{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection","id":949535,"title":"[Open Dev]Signs of Sorcery: Sheer Perfection!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-12T14:24:43-07:00","id":949535,"title":"[Open Dev]Signs of Sorcery: Sheer Perfection!","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/sheer-perfection-signs-of-sorcery-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\"> We have a new Open Dev!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T15:11:18-07:00","id":949559,"title":"","content":"Finally! Perfected materials and alchemy were two of my favourite parts of mage. These look pretty good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T15:35:03-07:00","id":949577,"title":"","content":"These are really cool and have a nice diversity of useful traits.<br /> I quite like the elaboration on the nature of perfected materials and how they extend beyond the archetypal set, even into the sinister and effective perfected flesh!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T15:40:41-07:00","id":949579,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I would not have expected for them to have what is traditionally the hardest material (adamant/Adamantium) be glass...and NOT the hardest material. I have no problem with that, just find it interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T15:51:27-07:00","id":949583,"title":"","content":"I'm so excited about this! I had to take breaks while reading, because I got too excited to sit still and read! This is amazing! I thought of a huge amount of questions while reading this, here are a few:<br /> <br /> Is &quot;...metal which scavenges Mana. Called 'dumanium'...&quot; a copy paste error? Does this material also scavenge mana like sophis?<br /> <br /> What does dumanium armor do?<br /> <br /> Does perfected fire require fuel or just oxygen? Can a patterning spell cause it to not need oxygen and or fuel? Or would that ruin the perfection and revert it to mundane fire?<br /> <br /> Can you perfect ephemera?<br /> <br /> Can you &quot;alloy&quot; the other non-metal perfected materials?<br /> <br /> Can you make perfected light and electricity?<br /> <br /> If make a lamp out of perfected materials does that emit perfected light?<br /> <br /> If you make a generator out of perfected materials, it the electricity perfected?<br /> <br /> Can you make a device which fires a perfected laser beam?<br /> <br /> Can you perfect silicon?<br /> <br /> Can you perfect data and programs?<br /> <br /> If a mage draws someone's blood, perfects it, then immediately put it back, what happens?<br /> <br /> If a mage surgically severs an arm, and perfects it, then surgically reattaches it, what happens?<br /> <br /> Edit: more questions<br /> <br /> If you set perfected wood on fire, does the fire become perfected?<br /> <br /> Are there perfected lodestones (or similar permanent magnets) that generate perfected magnetism?<br /> <br /> If you made an entire planetoid from perfected materials, would it have perfected gravity?<br /> <br /> Is there a perfected alloy (probably based on apeirion) that generates gravity in reasonable (non-planetoid) quantities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 08-12-2016, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T15:59:18-07:00","id":949586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949583#post949583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm so excited about this! I had to take breaks while reading, because I got too excited to sit still and read! This is amazing! I thought of a huge amount of questions while reading this, here are a few:<br /> <br /> Is &quot;...metal which scavenges Mana. Called 'dumanium'...&quot; a copy paste error? Does this material also scavenge mana like sophis?<br /> <br /> What does dumanium armor do?<br /> <br /> Does perfected fire require fuel or just oxygen? Can a patterning spell cause it to not need oxygen and or fuel? Or would that ruin the perfection and revert it to mundane fire?<br /> <br /> Can you perfect ephemera?<br /> <br /> Can you &quot;alloy&quot; the other non-metal perfected materials?<br /> <br /> Can you make perfected light and electricity?<br /> <br /> If make a lamp out of perfected materials does that emit perfected light?<br /> <br /> If you make a generator out of perfected materials, it the electricity perfected?<br /> <br /> Can you make a device which fires a perfected laser beam?<br /> <br /> Can you perfect silicon?<br /> <br /> Can you perfect data and programs?<br /> <br /> If a mage draws someone's blood, perfects it, then immediately put it back, what happens?<br /> <br /> If a mage surgically severs an arm, and perfects it, then surgically reattaches it, what happens?<br /> <br /> Edit: more questions<br /> <br /> If you set perfected wood on fire, does the fire become perfected?<br /> <br /> Are there perfected lodestones (or similar permanent magnets) that generate perfected magnetism?<br /> <br /> If you made an entire planetoid from perfected materials, would it have perfected gravity?<br /> <br /> Is there a perfected alloy (probably based on apeirion) that generates gravity in reasonable (non-planetoid) quantities?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mysteries! Mysteries everywhere!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T16:04:27-07:00","id":949592,"title":"","content":"First of all: yay, new spoilers! Thank you, Dave!<br /> And question about Dumanium: what is the benefit of using it as armor? It can have up to 5\\5 Armor rating, but you can replicate that with &quot;Aegis&quot; or even without magic at all. Yes, per point of Potency &quot;Forge Dumanium&quot; gives +1 to both general and ballistic armor ratings, while &quot;Aegis&quot; gives +1 to only one of them. But latter can be cast on existing armor, so enchanting simple kevlar vest is almost as potent as using alloy of Perfected metals.<br /> Dumanium weapons can use mana to make damage aggravated, but armor don't have &quot;spend mana&quot; option. Armor can be used as mana battery, but you can't move mana in or out without Prime 3, which also let you to just create tass.<br /> So, question is: was Dumanium intended to be mostly offensive material?<br /> Also, first sentence in spell description says about scavenging Mana, which is probably copy\\paste error from &quot;Forge Sophis&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11760,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11760-tauspher","user":"Tauspher","date":".  spelling 08-12-2016, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.c