],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T16:09:13-07:00","id":949597,"title":"","content":"hmmm,alloys... magical metal... BRANDON SANDERSON! Show yourself you beautiful bastard i read YOUR BOOK","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T16:27:01-07:00","id":949606,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the Wisdom sin for Perfected Blood is less if you only use yourself as a resource.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T16:27:39-07:00","id":949609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949583#post949583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage draws someone's blood, perfects it, then immediately put it back, what happens?<br /> <br /> If a mage surgically severs an arm, and perfects it, then surgically reattaches it, what happens?</div> </div> </div> </div>What if a mage does this to everything science knows how to remove and reattach (and even somethings that it can't if they have a Life mage on hand). <a href=\"http://www.newsweek.com/2016/05/06/first-human-head-transplant-452240.html\" target=\"_blank\">Which might include severing the head perfecting the body and putting it back.</a> They could do the same to large portions of the skull, and all the skin on the head.<br /> <br /> If attaching perfected parts works, then they could make someone whose body is over 90% perfected. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T16:35:28-07:00","id":949616,"title":"","content":"Also question: why is every way of making perfected blood and flesh should be Falling Wisdom sin? There is willing blood donors and you can probably get surgically removed tumor and perfect it. Bonus points if tumor was cancerous: you get yourself organic matter, perfect it, make tidy little book and inscribe your favorite rotes in it. And then by itself grimoire start to <i>grow</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11760-tauspher","name":"Tauspher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T16:39:46-07:00","id":949621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949609#post949609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What if a mage does this to everything science knows how to remove and reattach (and even somethings that it can't if they have a Life mage on hand). <a href=\"http://www.newsweek.com/2016/05/06/first-human-head-transplant-452240.html\" target=\"_blank\">Which might include severing the head perfecting the body and putting it back.</a> They could do the same to large portions of the skull, and all the skin on the head.<br /> <br /> If attaching perfected parts works, then they could make someone whose body is over 90% perfected.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They could even move the mind temporarily into a different body created for just a short while with a Life 4/5 spell and then perfect the at that point empty brain, or use other similar methods. Oh, the possibilities of modern science are endless. After all, 'impossible' is but a different word for 'challenge'.<br /> <br /> Although, admittedly, there is already a name for perfecting both body and soul - Ascension, perfecting just the body could have interesting and possibly somewhat unpredictable results. That's what makes it so interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T16:43:03-07:00","id":949623,"title":"","content":"No mithril? Sadness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T16:44:36-07:00","id":949624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tauspher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949616#post949616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also question: why is every way of making perfected blood and flesh should be Falling Wisdom sin? There is willing blood donors and you can probably get surgically removed tumor and perfect it. Bonus points if tumor was cancerous: you get yourself organic matter, perfect it, make tidy little book and inscribe your favorite rotes in it. And then by itself grimoire start to <i>grow</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://inc42.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/01/evil-ideas.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Welp, I'm not using that Mage when I introduce my gf to Mage, but I going to look for an excuse to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T16:47:07-07:00","id":949626,"title":"","content":"Siderite acts as Cold Iron against Changelings has just been basically confirmed, which gives mages a huge edge against Changelings and other Fae. It also makes Mage allies of great value to Changelings. <br /> <br /> Perfected Tin is my personal favourite, great for building swords, tools for summoning any kind of entity, and good for draining Emphreal enitities of essence. I'd makd it an Amlgam with perfect Mercury, but Mercury is poisonous (of course if perfected Mercury doesn't combined with anything that isn't perfected, then it can't poison you.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T16:59:59-07:00","id":949636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tauspher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949616#post949616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also question: why is every way of making perfected blood and flesh should be Falling Wisdom sin? There is willing blood donors and you can probably get surgically removed tumor and perfect it. Bonus points if tumor was cancerous: you get yourself organic matter, perfect it, make tidy little book and inscribe your favorite rotes in it. And then by itself grimoire start to <i>grow</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way i see it,Wisdom is all about being careful and not do anything too extreme,the highest wisdom mages are the ones who only use magic when absolutely necessary. using flesh and blood for a ritual even if they were donated to you,it's still a extreme and gory practice not the kind of thing Wisdom can shoulder well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T17:00:17-07:00","id":949637,"title":"","content":"Matter 3, Forces 3, massive aggravated damage. I have other thoughts, mostly boiling down to &quot;another way to make 1 dice yantras irrelevant&quot;, but I'm too tired now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T17:01:08-07:00","id":949638,"title":"","content":"As to the comment in the blog, I think keeping the spells as able to be Lasting is a good idea.<br /> <br /> At any rate, I really like what I've read so far. Some of it seems a little potent, but that's pretty typical for 2e it seems.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T17:31:14-07:00","id":949653,"title":"","content":"If your doing a liver transplant from a liver donar to a living patient, I could see turning the donated piece of liver into a perfect piece of liver, so that it never dies, does not get rejected by the body, never becomes cancerous, and works at top preformance.<br /> <br /> I could see a mage giving themselves a giant flesh tag to harvest it for making perfected flesh. <br /> <br /> A Mage could also castrate, including the sac, an enemy mage and make it perfected flesh, to make the perfect and most disturbing dildo ever *shudders* okay I'm having a nightmares tonight about that one.<br /> <br /> And people say Mage isn't a horror game *shudders*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T18:04:24-07:00","id":949668,"title":"","content":"Ingredients to making the best spaceship ever: siderite support structures, kassiterum hull, apeiron radiation shielding, brontium superconductors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T19:14:29-07:00","id":949708,"title":"","content":"Oooooooh man, do I ever want to make a werewolf hunter with a Lunargent sword. Or better yet, a Lunargent/Kassiterum Amalgam sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-12-2016, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T19:20:15-07:00","id":949709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949638#post949638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the comment in the blog, I think keeping the spells as able to be Lasting is a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually kind of like the idea of it not being able to be made Lasting. That way if you need a perfected metal in a hurry, you cast Hone the Perfected Form and get it right away, but it only stays perfected so long. A quick-and-dirty way of getting the material you need that seems fitting with the fact that the spell was created by &quot;impatient&quot; Libertines. If you want real, Lasting perfected metal, it's going to take time. You've got to seek out natural deposits, or go through the process of passing it in and out of Twilight. It lends some legitimacy to the old-fashioned crafting purists who insist on doing it &quot;the right way.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T19:30:25-07:00","id":949713,"title":"","content":"I'm with Charlaquin on not making the perfecting spells lasting, unless you want perfected metals to be plentiful. The implications of a quick reliable supply of perfected metals are . . . a headache. It's kind of like specialized enchanted items without the willpower dot cost to relinquish. Nothing wrong with it if you want that kind of campaign but I would subject such things to house rules myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T19:57:45-07:00","id":949744,"title":"","content":"I really don't like that you HAVE to have matter 3 in order to make the perfected form of anything. Why does perfected fire (something that should wholly be under the forces arcana) require matter 3 as well in order to be made. If it doesn't change I'm definitely going to homerule it so that you just need 3 dots of the relevant arcana to create the perfected form of a given substance (forces for fire or electricity or other energy, matter for matter, life for flesh, spirit or death for ephemera, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T20:34:32-07:00","id":949775,"title":"","content":"You dont have to have matter three to make perfected angthing. It just makes perfected metals more quickly. Forces should do fine for perfected fire and so on.<br /> <br /> I've thought about the consistency of the lasting reach effects a little more. I really don't like them. Take matter 4 transubstantiation for example. There is no lasting reach effect to turn lead into gold. Why should there be a lasting reach effect to turn iron into supernal iron? The errata recently nerfed platonic form to take away it's lasting reach effect. That effectively made lasting artificial tass impossible to mass produce with spells. I just don't think keeping the lasting reach effects on these spells is consistent with the way matter in particular is working. <br /> <br /> I think it would add to the mystique of an Atlantan ruin to find the whole place made of perfected metals, especially if records show there was once a way to produce them magically or if the world was once full of perfected metals but now only pockets survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T20:48:00-07:00","id":949785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949775#post949775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You dont have to have matter three to make perfected angthing. It just makes perfected metals more quickly. Forces should do fine for perfected fire and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The +2 reach effect of honing the perfected form disagrees with you. It openly states that to create perfected fire you have to spend 2 reach and use forces 3 as a conjunctural arcana on the base honing the perfected form spell. The perfected flesh section also says you just use honing the perfected form, not an alternate version of it using life 3 instead, which is what it should require.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:03:33-07:00","id":949794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949709#post949709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually kind of like the idea of it not being able to be made Lasting. That way if you need a perfected metal in a hurry, you cast Hone the Perfected Form and get it right away, but it only stays perfected so long. A quick-and-dirty way of getting the material you need that seems fitting with the fact that the spell was created by &quot;impatient&quot; Libertines. If you want real, Lasting perfected metal, it's going to take time. You've got to seek out natural deposits, or go through the process of passing it in and out of Twilight. It lends some legitimacy to the old-fashioned crafting purists who insist on doing it &quot;the right way.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, and it gives players a reason to do things properly.<br /> Yeah.<br /> I'm in the &quot;not Lasting&quot; camp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:59:36-07:00","id":949831,"title":"","content":"My general thought there is that it's a transformation into a new form, and that with enough effort, it shouldn't need to be 'upkept', it just takes on the new form. Plus, the general way it talks about it seems to imply that magic is sort of the preferred way now, not just something those impatient ol' libertines do, and I can't see that being the case if it can't be made Lasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:01:20-07:00","id":949833,"title":"","content":"Ah yes. because we never give up quality in our search for convenience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:13:55-07:00","id":949839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949831#post949831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My general thought there is that it's a transformation into a new form, and that with enough effort, it shouldn't need to be 'upkept', it just takes on the new form. Plus, the general way it talks about it seems to imply that magic is sort of the preferred way now, not just something those impatient ol' libertines do, and I can't see that being the case if it can't be made Lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong. It being Lasting does fit better with my understanding of what can and can't be made Lasting, and the text does suggest that adherence to tradition is really the only reason to do it the hard way any more. But the idea of there being benefits and drawbacks to either method appeals to my irrational human fairness-craving psychology and I'm willing to see the metaphysics bent a little bit here to appease those sensibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:21:43-07:00","id":949847,"title":"","content":"Definitely in the &quot;not lasting&quot; camp, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> has the right of it.<br /> <br /> Something I find very interesting is the implication that Mirrors are a fundamental Truth of the Universe, as you can Perfect a Mirror but no mention is made of needing to make it with other Perfected materials (e.g. Lunargent and Adamant) or what happens if the mirror is disassembled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:27:10-07:00","id":949852,"title":"","content":"Perfected glass weapons.<br /> <br /> That's it, I'm done. I have gotten what I've always wanted. You can stop writing books.<br /> <br /> Except, you know, for all the things I never knew I wanted. You can keep writing to give me that. You lot are very good at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:49:34-07:00","id":949865,"title":"","content":"Perfected Living Materials: For when you think its unfair that the Tremere got adapted from VtM to MtAw and the Tzimisce didn't.<br /> <br /> Because sometimes you just NEED a couch made from living human flesh. Or a throne. Or a cathedral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 08-13-2016, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:56:42-07:00","id":949867,"title":"","content":"Man, I always pick the wrong day to post homebrew stuff.<br /> <br /> I have thoughts on this but I just want to start out by saying I'm happy that perfected materials are finally Matter's provenance, rather than Matter + Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T23:34:06-07:00","id":949892,"title":"","content":"I'm not a fan of allowing Lasting perfecting effects, particularly since its accomplished with non-Mastery spells..On a practical player character level, it will create a great surfeit of perfected everything, potentially unbalancing parts of the setting and Paths. As a compromise, maybe make the procedures to create perfected materials just a <i>little</i> bit easier or quicker, or alternatively allow certain Time and Prime spells to expedite or ease the process.<br /> <br /> I also agree with the earlier posters' observations that there's no reason why Matter should be required to perfect items outside Matter's purview. Force's should be more than sufficient to perfect forces, Life for organic matter, etc., with the applicable Arcanum's Perfecting spells.<br /> <br /> I would also like to know if mages can perfect Platonic Forms? For instance, if a mage creates a platonic silver sword with Prime, can he then use Matter to &quot;super-perfect&quot; it to &quot;Platonic Lunargent.&quot; and if so, what would be the outcome or effect of both a perfected and platonic item? Further, can a mage with Prime just directly create a platonic form of an item made of a perfected substance, i.e., summon siderite sword?<br /> <br /> I'm additionally trying to imagine the nature of a myriad of other perfected substances and forces. For instance, how would you describe, and what would be the potential benefits, of things like perfected sunlight or electricity? What would perfected music sound like, etc.?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 08-13-2016, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T23:40:44-07:00","id":949893,"title":"","content":"&quot;Orichalcum&quot; means &quot;mountain copper&quot;. How did it become associated with gold?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T23:59:06-07:00","id":949903,"title":"","content":"If siderite can cut through anything, how would you make a scabbard for a siderite sword?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T00:15:07-07:00","id":949915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949709#post949709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want real, Lasting perfected metal, it's going to take time. You've got to seek out natural deposits, or go through the process of passing it in and out of Twilight. It lends some legitimacy to the old-fashioned crafting purists who insist on doing it &quot;the right way.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily a negative, but that's gonna make Moros the worst crafters of perfected materials.<br /> There are two Arcana that can can create gateways to Twilight that you can repeatedly carry items across, Death and Spirit. Spirit is the Moros' inferior Arcanum, and you can't use Death because it doesn't just transform items into Twilight, it actually destroys them. So a Moros cannot use Death for that, and they are bad at Spirit.<br /> Once you take the abillity to create lasting perfected materials away from Matter (ironic in its own way) Moros are left with the worst toolset for making it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T00:18:39-07:00","id":949917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949915#post949915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not necessarily a negative, but that's gonna make Moros the worst crafters of perfected materials.<br /> There are two Arcana that can can create gateways to Twilight that you can repeatedly carry items across, Death and Spirit. Spirit is the Moros' inferior Arcanum, and you can't use Death because it doesn't just transform items into Twilight, it actually destroys them. So a Moros cannot use Death for that, and they are bad at Spirit.<br /> Once you take the abillity to create lasting perfected materials away from Matter (ironic in its own way) Moros are left with the worst toolset for making it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't the +1 Reach effect on Ghost Gate allow you to take items into Twilight without destroying them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T00:25:02-07:00","id":949918,"title":"","content":"If all it takes to make perfected metals is passing it into and out of Twilight then couldn't Beasts do it too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7525-quinn-h","name":"Quinn H.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T00:28:52-07:00","id":949920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949903#post949903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If siderite can cut through anything, how would you make a scabbard for a siderite sword?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scabbards are designed to hold a sword by its quillons, not by its tip or edge. In a normal sword, carrying a sword by its tip would dull the blade, defeating most of the point of having a scabbard around your sword to begin with.<br /> <br /> You may as well ask how you would hold a siderite sword, since it'd cut through your hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T00:38:17-07:00","id":949922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949915#post949915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not necessarily a negative, but that's gonna make Moros the worst crafters of perfected materials.<br /> There are two Arcana that can can create gateways to Twilight that you can repeatedly carry items across, Death and Spirit. Spirit is the Moros' inferior Arcanum, and you can't use Death because it doesn't just transform items into Twilight, it actually destroys them. So a Moros cannot use Death for that, and they are bad at Spirit.<br /> Once you take the abillity to create lasting perfected materials away from Matter (ironic in its own way) Moros are left with the worst toolset for making it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They've got Matter as ruling though, making them the best at creating perfected materials <i>quickly</i>. Besides, they can use Ghost Gate to shift the material Twilight and Touchbof the Grave to bring it back. Or summon or create a Ghost with the Gateway Manifestaton and pass the material in and out of the Underworld. Or use Open Avernian Gate and pass the material in and out of the underworld.<br /> <br /> Between Matter and Death, this would make Moros by far <i>the best</i> at creating perfected materials, since they have two different ruling Arcanum that can be used to make them, in different ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T00:40:49-07:00","id":949925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinn H.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949918#post949918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If all it takes to make perfected metals is passing it into and out of Twilight then couldn't Beasts do it too</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about Beasts, but Werewolves sure could. I imagine there are probably some Firetouched who carry silver weapons and pass in and out of Shadow often enough they probably end up with Lunargent weapons <i>by accident</i>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T00:42:02-07:00","id":949928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949920#post949920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scabbards are designed to hold a sword by its quillons, not by its tip or edge. In a normal sword, carrying a sword by its tip would dull the blade, defeating most of the point of having a scabbard around your sword to begin with.<br /> <br /> You may as well ask how you would hold a siderite sword, since it'd cut through your hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but even if it's not bearing the weight on its blade, it can still shift in the scabbard, and any slight bump to the inside of the scabbard will cut through it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T00:45:47-07:00","id":949930,"title":"","content":"I don't care that much about whether the effects of spells are Lasting or not (although I like the idea that spells are the quicker and easier, but not Lasting, Libertines are such plebs). However I care about whether there is a way, albeit a difficult one, that allows you to have an alloy/amalgam that is Lasting. If you look at the Alloys and Amalgams sections again, it seems to me that magically created alloys and non magical Hermium amalgams are substances with distinct unoverlapping effects. You either non-magically create an amalgam, where you get the combined effects of multiple perfected substances <i>or</i> you use magic to combine them, lose the original properties and gain the new ones.<br /> <br /> Ideal solution would be to either clarify that Amalgams keep the original effects on top of getting the new effect by combining the substances (that would also make them better than conventional spells) and that the spells are simply a quicker and less effective way of doing things (whether you want the spells to be Lasting or not. Although if they aren't, maybe the purists shouldn't be regarded as only doing things out of habit.).<br /> <br /> The other option would be to keep the division, but have the spells keep the Lasting option, so that you can even have Thaumium that is undispellable. These solutions would keep the usefulness of all the methods and you wouldn't have to be pissed off every time an enemy Asshole Obrimos dispells your Dumanium armor.<br /> <br /> Because frankly, stories are full of &quot;breaking through wards&quot;, &quot;dispelling spells&quot; and &quot;turning people to their true form&quot; by in some way ending the spell, but I have yet to encounter a story where you &quot;dispel&quot; Excalibur's magical powers and render it to be just a sharp trophy. There may be stories like that, but they really aren't that common. Undispellable Adamantium, Dragonsteel, Starmetal and whatnot are pretty much the standard.<br /> <br /> tl;dr: Let's make sure there is at least one way, by which can any given type of perfected substance or their combination be made Lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 08-13-2016, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T00:47:35-07:00","id":949931,"title":"","content":"Some quick thoughts:<br /> <br /> * Seems a bit &quot;catalogue-y&quot;. Here are the major known perfected forms, here's what they do, here's how you make them . . . Seems to lack that certain element of mystery and wonder. Particularly when a number of the perfected metals have the same basic properties - seems more atmospheric to focus on the exceptions, and the speculation on why they're the exceptions. Might want to look into more poetic/mystical names for the non-metals, too<br /> <br /> * It also seems like there should be cultural/Legacy issues in play. If nothing else, the Elemental Masteries should probably have strong opinions on things like perfected fire and water. <br /> <br /> * Shouldn't items like perfected mirrors pick up more metaphysical properties, too? Like maybe showing the truth of the person's soul (<i>a la</i> the Frog Prince/Hans the Iron Giant), or make it easier to teleport/scry/enter Shadow?<br /> <br /> * As for the Free Council's new way to make perfected metals . . . yeah, I'm not wild about it. The idea that a &quot;quick fix&quot; is better than the traditional way seems odd, particularly given the context. Its not a matter of duration - what bothers me is that the result is equal to doing it the long, slow, &quot;natural&quot; way.<br /> <br /> And there is precedent. If you look at real world efforts to artificially reproduce diamonds, we've had quite a bit of success - from cubic zirconia to industrially manufactured ones. However, people generally feel that even the best synthetic diamonds are somehow inferior to the &quot;real&quot; thing. Even if its purely for cosmetic purposes, an artificial diamond just doesn't measure up. <br /> <br /> Seems like the Free Council's method might be a way to build on that intuition. That the perfected metals their rote produces are somhow inferior - not as high bonuses, missing properties, don't last as long . . . <br /> <br /> Plus, given that the Free Council prides itself on being both the heirs of the ancient Nameless, <i>and</i> the mages who pioneered the search for the new magic, seems like there should be pretty serious internal disputes over whether the classic or modern method is better.<br /> <br /> * Building on the idea of this being the Fallen World, it might be worth playing around with an antagonistic phenomena. Something that actively decays/corrupts perfected elements<br /> <br /> * Not quite sold on the name &quot;Brontium&quot; for perfected copper. My alchemy's a little rusty ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), so I'm not sure if that's a historical name, but it sounds a bit too much like a scientific element, off the periodic table <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tauspher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949616#post949616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also question: why is every way of making perfected blood and flesh should be Falling Wisdom sin? There is willing blood donors and you can probably get surgically removed tumor and perfect it. Bonus points if tumor was cancerous . .</div> </div> </div> </div>So then we'd have magical super cancer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you're looking for a really nightmarish magical organic artifact, take a look at the Speaking Gun (particularly the version the future Suzy Shooter has) in Simon R. Greene's <i>Nightside</i> series. A weapon created by chopping up some poor bastard, and sewing him back together in the shape of a gun, it can kill anything. And it wants to, too - its in horrible pain, and the only way it can know peace is if the universe is destroyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T01:02:19-07:00","id":949936,"title":"","content":"So if you make a still out of Brontium, do you get perfected booze?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949931#post949931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite sold on the name &quot;Brontium&quot; for perfected copper. My alchemy's a little rusty ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), so I'm not sure if that's a historical name, but it sounds a bit too much like a scientific element, off the periodic table</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Bront&quot; means &quot;Thunder&quot;. It may have associations with &quot;Bhrem&quot;, meaning &quot;to growl&quot;. &quot;Brontes&quot;, son of Uranus and Gaia, was one of three <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyclops\" target=\"_blank\">Cyclopses</a> described by Hesiod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-13-2016, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T01:53:40-07:00","id":949940,"title":"","content":"Repost of comment under blog post:<br /> <br /> <b>I'm a bit confused why <i>only</i> Free Council could 'hammer out' ( pun intendent <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) spell to make Metal into Perfected.</b> We literally have 2,5 thousands of years for Iron Age mages to XIX century on very common topic to work and experiment on that. I would understand if it would be like Atomic Power, that is very new phenomena - but one ancient and popular as such should not be limited to Libertines reverse engineering only.<br /> <br /> As to <i>Hone the Perfected Form </i>spell itself - <b>I would take out Lasting option. It still can be made Indefinite with advanced Matter mage and it would also not made whole 'Twilight and back' process meaningless.</b> Then process become the Lasting solution. I want to point out also the Indefinite Perfecting of metals can have very interesting story implications when they become Havocs... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> OR we assume that 'Twilight and back' is more Sleepers and apprentices thing UNTIL they get / hit Matter 3 and then they just cast it all the time.<br /> <br /> Side question: <b>Would Perfected Metals react somehow to Prometheans on Refinement connected to original Metal?</b> Like that Plumbum ( Iron ) Created can be somehow detected by the Siderite? It would make interesting crossover idea, I think. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-13-2016, 04:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T02:25:20-07:00","id":949946,"title":"","content":"Idea - <b>Perfected organic materials ( like blood or skin ) are 'alive' and items from them can 'heal' or even 'regenerate' in longer periods of time.</b> Cursed tome of black magic made from human skin and blood is nearly indestructible, it just 'grows back' any than the most profound damage to it. ( <i>Evil Dead</i> series and it's Necronomicon comes to mind! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T02:30:44-07:00","id":949948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949940#post949940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Repost of comment under blog post:<br /> <br /> <b>I'm a bit confused why <i>only</i> Free Council could 'hammer out' ( pun intendent <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) spell to make Metal into Perfected.</b> We literally have 2,5 thousands of years for Iron Age mages to XIX century on very common topic to work and experiment on that. I would understand if it would be like Atomic Power, that is very new phenomena - but one ancient and popular as such should not be limited to Libertines reverse engineering only.</div> </div> </div> </div>The libertines probably wouldn't have been the first and only group. Lore gets lost over the years afterall, as do grimoires and knowledge of spells, the libertines just developed their own version of it through a lack of caring about &quot;sticking to the old way of doing things&quot; and created the newest incarnation of the spell, unknowingly replicating the works of the great alchemist Sir Elric Smith a renowned metalworker and moros of the medieval era whose work with perfected iron, including spells to haste the process of creation, was sadly lost in a great fire just after the crusades began however some of the objects he forged can still be found in the hands of mages today passed on from master to student over the centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T02:56:39-07:00","id":949953,"title":"","content":"Besides everything that I already mentioned in my post, I'm also a fan of spells that do not make a material perfected on their own, but help with the process - like various Time spells or specialized spells made specifically to transfer materials between material/twilight/shadow/underworld/hedge/whatever.<br /> <br /> Also, can you combine all the metals as an Alloy/Amalgam and if yes, what is the result? I remember reading something about Electrum, which would be the result, but I can't remember whether it was something Dave mentioned or a homebrew of some sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T03:20:16-07:00","id":949955,"title":"","content":"Will there be clarification as to how Perfected Materials interact with Enhanced Item, Imbued Item and Grimoire Merits?<br /> <br /> I love the material already. Especially the part about living materials. I am surprised that they're treated as as much a transgression as destroying Souls. Causing deliberate death and long-term injury are sins against Understanding Wisdom. Using consensually removed samples sounds like an Enlightened Wisdom sin at worst, due to rubbing shoulders with dodgy symbolism. If they're to be classified as dark magic, their harmfulness needs to be slightly better explained. Even acknowledging that Mages are surprised how corrupting it is would be helpful.<br /> <br /> Also, do dead materials give perfected leather, bone and wood, or are they obscure and shunned? The text seems to claim both. I'm also confused about perfected bones. Are living bones any different from dead ones? If not, the text on perfected bones could essentially be moved to the list of Other Materials. <br /> <br /> Additionally, I think Alkahest needs a word of clarification. As written, it could be considered to dissolve containers, rocks and careless Mages.<br /> <br /> Seeing another effect given a Lasting duration just reminds me how I don't understand which spells deserve it, which don't, and which cause persistent changes by default. Signs of Sorcery is the best book to clarify it, but it's a large undertaking. I love the system and not being able to grasp this is frustrating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T04:11:07-07:00","id":949972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949953#post949953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides everything that I already mentioned in my post, I'm also a fan of spells that do not make a material perfected on their own, but help with the process - like various Time spells or specialized spells made specifically to transfer materials between material/twilight/shadow/underworld/hedge/whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by the general dislike people have of the Lasting Reach option how about a different approach: Take away the Reach option to make it lasting from the Matter spell and instead provide a +1 Reach option that halves the amount of neccesary passes through Twilight. You could even make it possible to take that option multiple times. That way you would have a way to speed up the traditional process, which would still fit the current hasty Libertine background, while not providing the world with a large heap of Perfected metals created by everyone that has access to the Rote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T04:11:14-07:00","id":949973,"title":"","content":"Is Perfected Leather as absurd as it seems? It seems to grant immunity to Bashing damage at the very least, and possibly Lethal damage from bludgeoning/crushing-related sources (e.g. being hit with a sledgehammer).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T04:45:19-07:00","id":949980,"title":"","content":"There is also one more reason to NOT making Lasting <i>Hone the Perfect Form</i> spell - that then Forge Masters Legacy have much more sense as<b> 'special Perfected smiths'</b>. Only their Attainments ( based on taking this spell ) would let you created large quantities of Perfected Metals in matters of hours, instead of days as normal - that is what it <i>should</i> be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Reach option for halving necessary times is interesting one, I must agree. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949948#post949948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The libertines probably wouldn't have been the first and only group. Lore gets lost over the years afterall, as do grimoires and knowledge of spells, the libertines just developed their own version of it through a lack of caring about &quot;sticking to the old way of doing things&quot; and created the newest incarnation of the spell, unknowingly replicating the works of the great alchemist Sir Elric Smith a renowned metalworker and moros of the medieval era whose work with perfected iron, including spells to haste the process of creation, was sadly lost in a great fire just after the crusades began however some of the objects he forged can still be found in the hands of mages today passed on from master to student over the centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not for mages - if some technique is semi-popular in some circles, it has Astral Realm of it in Temenos and so can be rediscover time and time again. After few repetition it's just becomes Orders standard.<br /> <br /> I want to also point that metallurgy is one of basic technologies of human civilization from times of 1000 BCE to around 1800 CE - thinking that mages would omit time and again this great magical Mystery field is just irrational thinking about setting. This Perfecting spell at least should be popular in times of Alexander Empire where new alloys were tested by Sleepers.<br /> <br /> If there is spell about something, we have maybe few years window before some Awakened makes it standard ( see example with Nuclear power in <b>Imperial Mysteries </b>). Surely not about 3000 years as text is implying.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-13-2016, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T04:46:40-07:00","id":949981,"title":"","content":"Since I've been thinking about a medically-aspected Mage recently, I'd like to see an alloy of perhaps Lunargent and Perfected Chromium to create a metal that always remains medically sterile and never tarnishes, and perhaps grants a Yantra bonus to magic of a curative nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8871-griffalo","name":"griffalo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8871_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T05:22:04-07:00","id":949985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949623#post949623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No mithril? Sadness</div> </div> </div> </div>Mithril was described as being silvered steel. So a lunargent steel alloy maybe? Or even just moonsilver itself could be mithril for this verse. <br /> <br /> <br /> Overall, I love the new stuff <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I'm of the opinion that the spells should not have the option to be made Lasting.<br /> Both because this would trivialise making perfected materials and thus everyone and their familiar would have lunargent bracelets and daggers and whatnot, and because I like the way this trend of moving away from Lasting allows for Legacies that do things not normally possible, i.e. their Indefinite effects are effectively Lasting (no dispel no paradox no anything)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T05:24:31-07:00","id":949986,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think I'm going to remove the Lasting effect on Hone The Perfected Form; if you want a Perfected item that won't eventually revert, you have to make it the old-fashioned way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T05:31:23-07:00","id":949992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949986#post949986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think I'm going to remove the Lasting effect on Hone The Perfected Form; if you want a Perfected item that won't eventually revert, you have to make it the old-fashioned way.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be pretty neat.<br /> <br /> That said, the existing traditional method is both a bit too slow and.. eh.. boring. Not mystical enough.<br /> I'm okay with it staying as described, but would be happier if it needed some preparation in chemical/alchemical solutions between passes, or some such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T05:47:10-07:00","id":949996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949986#post949986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think I'm going to remove the Lasting effect on Hone The Perfected Form; if you want a Perfected item that won't eventually revert, you have to make it the old-fashioned way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will just remind here the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12164_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12164\" data-vbnamecard=\"12164\">Zaephyrus</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949972#post949972\">proposition</a> - adding Reach option to half amount of neccesary passes through Twilight - it would make those Matter Masters create Perfected Metals <i>really </i>quick, but also not making it just *poof, Lasting* middle ground of debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-13-2016, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T05:58:50-07:00","id":949997,"title":"","content":"I pretty much agree with Dave and Seidmadr. The removal of Lasting effect on Hone the Perfected Form would make the process of making basic unalloyed unamalgamated (is that even a word?) Lasting materials much harder. On the other hand, as long as Patterning Matter spells that create alloys retain the Lasting effect, it will still allow mages to create Lasting alloys like Thaumium (which we need to remember are different from nonmagically created amalgams) and give them a niche that no other supernatural group can fulfill, thus making sure that (advanced) perfected materials like alloys are quintessentially a mage thing and not something any Joe the cleaner could do.<br /> <br /> The preparation before the transfer would also do 2 things: Make the process more mysterious and further define mages as a group most likely to know of it (although in this case, the basic perfected materials may have the option to be created by other beings, depending on the alchemical processes used. A good material for, say, a crossover book, don't you think?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T06:25:51-07:00","id":950001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949985#post949985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mithril was described as being silvered steel. So a lunargent steel alloy maybe? Or even just moonsilver itself could be mithril for this verse.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmmm.... Lunargent and Siderite alloy... what would be the properties, though? Mithril writings turned invisible when not exposed to moonlight, lightweight, and... hm...? Use mana to increase the sharpness and speed (initiative bonus)? Concealment bonus? Would make a good assassin-style weapon if so...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T06:29:51-07:00","id":950002,"title":"","content":"Question on amalgams. It seems that perfected mercury reacts to other perfected items so you can shape them into specific shapes, then hardens, and retains properties of the original metals.<br /> <br /> Does the fluid nature of mercury remain on the amalgam? Or is it basically just a solid object now with a +2 shapeshift yanta bonus and new shape?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T06:57:12-07:00","id":950008,"title":"","content":"It's not that big an issue, but I'd like some vague explanation of why passing the element into Twilight perfects something. It feels kinda odd that in comparison natural perfected materials appear at Hallows, which makes sense, seeing as they're materials related to the Supernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T06:57:37-07:00","id":950009,"title":"","content":"Nitpick: Greek for &quot;power&quot; is &quot;dunamis,&quot; so it should really be &quot;Dunamium.&quot; Or &quot;Dynamium,&quot; but that might sound a bit too sciencey. (I know you said no spelling errors, but this seems like the kind of thing an editor could easily miss.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T07:52:02-07:00","id":950030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949955#post949955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, I think Alkahest needs a word of clarification. As written, it could be considered to dissolve containers, rocks and careless Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually really surprised that adamant didn't have the property of being insoluble in alkahest. I thought it would be natural that if you want to safely contain perfected acid, you need a vial of perfected glass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thanke