es imply them.</div> </div> </div> </div>...to be immune to its effects.<br /> <br /> I need to pay more attention to what I write.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T09:32:23-07:00","id":950092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950077#post950077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...to be immune to its effects.<br /> <br /> I need to pay more attention to what I write.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it implies that some sort of non-mundane material is immune to it. It's so vague about what though. I didn't get the get the impression that all perfected materials were supposed to be immune.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T09:32:39-07:00","id":950093,"title":"","content":"I just noticed that studying Perfected substances shows a &quot;strong connection&quot; to a given Supernal realm,<br /> <br /> Is this an <i>actual</i> Strong sympathetic link?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T10:00:46-07:00","id":950108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950092#post950092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it implies that some sort of non-mundane material is immune to it. It's so vague about what though. I didn't get the get the impression that all perfected materials were supposed to be immune.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another bit in need of clarity, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T10:12:50-07:00","id":950116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949922#post949922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They've got Matter as ruling though, making them the best at creating perfected materials <i>quickly</i>. Besides, they can use Ghost Gate to shift the material Twilight and Touchbof the Grave to bring it back. Or summon or create a Ghost with the Gateway Manifestaton and pass the material in and out of the Underworld. Or use Open Avernian Gate and pass the material in and out of the underworld.<br /> <br /> Between Matter and Death, this would make Moros by far <i>the best</i> at creating perfected materials, since they have two different ruling Arcanum that can be used to make them, in different ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Matter as ruling doesn't help with creating lasting perfected materials, though I give you that it can suffice in a pinch. The same trick Moros can do with Ghosts Thyrsus can do with Spirits and Mastigos with Goetia.<br /> <br /> Calling them &quot;by far <i>the best</i>&quot; is absolutely debatable here and I disagree. At best, I'd call them third place. Thyrsus are easily the best creators of lasting perfected materials, having access to both the best direct Twilight Gate power, and just as easy access to ephemerals with the Gateway manifestation. Mastigos and Moros are tied for second place, with Mastigos slightly ahead as they don't have Spirit as inferior Arcanum which allows independence from ephemerals for perfected metal creation. Acanthus and Obrimos bring up the rear.<br /> <br /> Moros don't have two Arcana that can create Perfected Materials. They have one that create dispellable perfected materials (big weakness), and another that can create lasting perfected Material <i>indirectly</i> via using Ghosts (which is either expensive if you have trade for the Gateway, or a Wisdom Sin if you order its use).<br /> <br /> Touch of the Grave doesn't help create Perfected Materials. Once it passes through the Ghost Gate, the item is destroyed. Touch of the Grave can pull it over, but even then the item is made of ephemera, no longer of its original material.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I hope this post doesn't read as more aggressive than I intend. As a Moros player, I am just a bit irritated that the Matter Path gets to be so bad at interacting with and creating perfected Matter. We have played for 50 sessions, so I can be absolutely sure when I say there is zero chance of my character wasting either a spell control slot or xp on having something made of perfected metal via Matter Spell (they are not <i>that</i> good), and having to depend on a Ghost to create it instead of doing it yourself just feels utterly wrong.<br /> Really, I just want that 'Ghost Gate destroys Items' thing to be removed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 08-13-2016, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T10:37:41-07:00","id":950133,"title":"","content":"Interesting note - because Adamant is perfectly transparent, you can't make working spectacles out of them.<br /> <br /> Also, I am definitely going to have some low wisom Libertines who incorporate perfected living materials into machines<br /> <br /> &quot;...hey, Genesis, why does the computer seem to have a <i>beating heart</i>?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T10:38:47-07:00","id":950134,"title":"","content":"Two words: Perfected Food.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T10:53:34-07:00","id":950144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950134#post950134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two words: Perfected Food.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now <i>that's</i> a character concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T10:54:50-07:00","id":950145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950116#post950116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Touch of the Grave doesn't help create Perfected Materials. Once it passes through the Ghost Gate, the item is destroyed. Touch of the Grave can pull it over, but even then the item is made of ephemera, no longer of its original material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... So it is. My bad, I misinterpreted that interaction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950116#post950116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: I hope this post doesn't read as more aggressive than I intend. As a Moros player, I am just a bit irritated that the Matter Path gets to be so bad at interacting with and creating perfected Matter. We have played for 50 sessions, so I can be absolutely sure when I say there is zero chance of my character wasting either a spell control slot or xp on having something made of perfected metal via Matter Spell (they are not <i>that</i> good), and having to depend on a Ghost to create it instead of doing it yourself just feels utterly wrong.<br /> Really, I just want that 'Ghost Gate destroys Items' thing to be removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, you're good, man.<br /> <br /> Don't forget, at Death 5 you can use Create Avernian Gate to pass the material in and out of the underworld, which also works. And honestly, I think it's more than reasonable to make a Death spell that lets you pass an object in and out of Twilight without destroying its physical form with Creative Thaumaturgy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T11:02:49-07:00","id":950150,"title":"","content":"I have an alternate idea for Perfecting materials!<br /> <br /> Unfortunately it just goes &quot;something, something, soul stones, something&quot;. And I'm not sure what those somethings are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T11:20:48-07:00","id":950155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950150#post950150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an alternate idea for Perfecting materials!<br /> <br /> Unfortunately it just goes &quot;something, something, soul stones, something&quot;. And I'm not sure what those somethings are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Matter + Death spell to make an amalgamation of an object with a soulstone, thus creating a perfected metal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T11:28:29-07:00","id":950158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950155#post950155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Matter + Death spell to make an amalgamation of an object with a soulstone, thus creating a perfected metal</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it should require spells, though.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b><br /> <br /> Well, duh. Now I feel dumb.<br /> <br /> Make the soul stone - it has to be composed of metals associated to your Path's realm (unless you have Matter/Prime trickery going on). We then steal the process for increasing Wisdom, and have purifying the metal take an Obsession, a Story worth of work at it, and 2xp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 08-13-2016, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T13:24:00-07:00","id":950196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950134#post950134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two words: Perfected Food.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Cellular Nutrition chef.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T13:37:42-07:00","id":950201,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of these perfected materials (though one or two felt very flat). I think I'd really enjoy introducing them yo my chronicle, especially with a Moros Free Council engineer in my party. What worries me, though, is that they're so bloody useful (lunargent reflecting twilight!!) that even removing the Lasting option, I can't help but think they'd be extremely pervasive for sale anywhere the Orders are prevalent. I mean, of course the consillium big wigs have thaumium regalia and sindirite swords.<br /> So I'm torn between really wanting to use these, but needing a reason for them to be nigh omnipresent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T13:54:03-07:00","id":950205,"title":"","content":"Step 1: Grab your desired material.<br /> Step 2: Make it smaller, turning it into Size 0 object using Shrink and Grow<br /> Step 3: Pass it once in and out of Twilight<br /> Step 4: Congratulations, permanent perfected material<br /> Step 5: Dispel Shrink and Grow<br /> <br /> If you feel that's cheesy, then make it Size 1, reduce it's Durability to 1, and pass it 10 times in and out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-13-2016, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T14:27:42-07:00","id":950224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950205#post950205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Step 1: Grab your desired material.<br /> Step 2: Make it smaller, turning it into Size 0 object using Shrink and Grow<br /> Step 3: Pass it once in and out of Twilight<br /> Step 4: Congratulations, permanent perfected material<br /> Step 5: Dispel Shrink and Grow<br /> <br /> If you feel that's cheesy, then make it Size 1, reduce it's Durability to 1, and pass it 10 times in and out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just break it into sand sized grains. Each grain is now a size 0 object. Simply pour bags of the stuff through two stacked twilight conversion portals into a bin beneath them.<br /> <br /> You can even automate the process, just enchant a couple of hoops, one converts all physical things passing through it into twilight, the other turns them back again. At this point you can seal these together into a tube, conceal it in a larger machine then have sleeper employees (who don't know what they are really doing) and machines run a factory producing the stuff. Or you could replace the sleepers with golems, I guess, but that would make this require more than two spells/imbuements. Or with sufficient technical aptitude you could use robots in place of sleepers.<br /> <br /> You could make the hoops really long, with many tubes attached funneling things through it and many parallel operations running side by side. You could have say a dozen inputs and outputs (input 1 connects to output 1, input 2 connects to output 2, etc) each with conveyor belts attached.<br /> <br /> This automation method even works if the formula is based on higher of size or 1 instead of size, you just need to keep track of how many times a batch has been put through the machine. And raw materials would be easier to procure as I'm pretty sure large pellets/small ingots of metals are more common than metal that has been reduced to sand sized grains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T14:42:08-07:00","id":950229,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm absolutely in love with those perfected materials and I really hope the Lasting option remains in the game. Mostly because I prefer more options to few options. Also a single point needs to be made.<br /> <br /> 1) Living Materials require using the spell the moment the seperation happens, if the spell can not be made lasting, living material can never be permanent, since it would require several non-instant steps to turn them perfect.<br /> <br /> Also, its entirely possible to wear a leather jacket, made out of your own skin. Possibly tattoed with high speech. Surely flaying yourself to turn your own skin into a perfected living material can not be a sin against wisdom :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI have long since forsaken mortal blood. It offers me nothing but the stale taste of mayflies. I have partaken of Luna's ever-changing children and dined on the scholars of Magic. I have bled monsters, born and created. No more. Tonight I drink the blood of gods and slake my thirst for another thousand years of night.\u201d","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/312-grunt","name":"Grunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T14:50:49-07:00","id":950230,"title":"","content":"WHW, your proposition seems wrong. Clever, but wrong. Not really sure why it shouldn't work though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> The listed way of creating Perfected Materials &quot;naturally&quot; doesn't seen that difficult. Somewhat time-consuming, sure, but it seems like you could easily make a system to ease the making.<br /> In a room in your Sanctum you have a desk with two rods, and the lump of material you want Perfected. (or item already made of said material I guess). Every day, you have a Retainer go into the room, use first one rod then othe other on the lump, ten times.<br /> The first rod has a custom effect that shifts the target into Twilight. The second rod (in addition to being enspelled to be able to interact with Twilight stuff) brings the target out of Twilight into our lovely reality.<br /> Or just do it yourself every morning. You get up, do your morning bathroom routine, pass the lump into and out of Twilight ten times, then go on with your day.<br /> <br /> The spells written down in the book may not be too friendly for this task, but they're just guidelines, surely you can do some nice twisting of Death or Spirit to achieve a &quot;check it, Twilight!&quot; effect. And the second rod may not even be needed. The spell could just have a short duration and the item would come back from Twilight on its own?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Seems Custos Tenebrarum beat me to posting a system, and did it in a nice manufacturing way, most cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11842,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","user":"Aeryes","date":".  bygones 08-13-2016, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T14:52:13-07:00","id":950231,"title":"","content":"Rather than always employing the passing through Twilight process to create perfected metals, I imagine a great many powerful cabals control or have significant interests in mines across the globe, and if parts of such mines are within a powerful hallow as may be created by a mage with Prime 5, I assume that there are at least a few regular and reliable sources of perfected metals, although the prices. financial and otherwise, to obtain the material might be <i>very</i> expensive or even a plot hook in itself.<br /> <br /> I also agree with a prior poster that the text requires some explanation as to why metals become perfected when passing often between twilight and the material other than a few words about how they are &quot;cleansed.&quot; It seems we just take it for granted that it's necessary, without any accompanying metaphysics that could be applied to the process through the use of other Arcana.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I'm very surprised that Prime appears to have absolutely nothing to do with &quot;perfecting&quot; substances given its redefined and emphasized purview (and I would love an answer to my earlier question concerning platonic forms and perfected materials)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T15:01:32-07:00","id":950236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950231#post950231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, I'm very surprised that Prime appears to have absolutely nothing to do with &quot;perfecting&quot; substances given its redefined and emphasized purview (and I would love an answer to my earlier question concerning platonic forms and perfected materials)..</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also like a way to perfect substances with Prime; I agree that that seems like something that Prime should be able to do. Perhaps casting Ephemeral Enchanantment on the substance repeatedly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T15:20:42-07:00","id":950248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950231#post950231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, I'm very surprised that Prime appears to have absolutely nothing to do with &quot;perfecting&quot; substances given its redefined and emphasized purview (and I would love an answer to my earlier question concerning platonic forms and perfected materials)..</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Perfecting is a Practice, not an Arcanum purview. By definition any Arcanum can Perfect something under its purview. Perfecting a substance through Matter should give it stronger, more startling properties, while Perfecting through Prime should be able to make it closer to a pure symbol-form. If I were to CT this stuff myself I'd probably have, for example, the &quot;cuts through anything, ignores durability&quot; aspect of Sidarite conferred by a Matter spell, and the &quot;incredibly good yantra for strengthening and protection spells&quot; aspect be Prime? Then again, just being a rare, special material in the first place makes it useful as a yantra. Maybe Prime to have it add a +2 bonus to anything symbolically resonant with Iron, as it's Perfecting it as a symbol of iron?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T15:41:55-07:00","id":950269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950248#post950248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Perfecting is a Practice, not an Arcanum purview. By definition any Arcanum can Perfect something under its purview. Perfecting a substance through Matter should give it stronger, more startling properties, while Perfecting through Prime should be able to make it closer to a pure symbol-form. If I were to CT this stuff myself I'd probably have, for example, the &quot;cuts through anything, ignores durability&quot; aspect of Sidarite conferred by a Matter spell, and the &quot;incredibly good yantra for strengthening and protection spells&quot; aspect be Prime? Then again, just being a rare, special material in the first place makes it useful as a yantra. Maybe Prime to have it add a +2 bonus to anything symbolically resonant with Iron, as it's Perfecting it as a symbol of iron?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Any Arcanum <i>cannot</i> perfect something according to Dave's spoilers. All perfecting apparently now requires Matter 3, with the possible <i>additional</i> use of Forces or Life (see Reach effects for Hone the Perfected Form and the text of Living Materials). I believe this should be changed and work as you, as well as I and others, earlier suggest.<br /> <br /> Further, &quot;perfecting&quot; materials in the context of this discussion means creating a sympathetic or stronger semiotic link with a supernal realm(s). This, in my estimation, seems precisely like the purview of Prime regardless of the material or item to be affected (with the possible need to add the relevant pattern Arcana of Matter, Forces or Life to the spell).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":"08-13-2016, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T18:33:48-07:00","id":950358,"title":"","content":"Any Arcana can Perfect <i>examples of things under its purview</i>. That's what the Perfecting Practice does. The question is, is the process of turning (say) gold to orichalcum a matter of refining the molecular structure of the gold, or a matter of bringing the gold symbolically more in line with its supernal ideal? If it's the former, it should be Matter Perfecting. If it's the latter, it should be Prime Perfecting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T18:38:57-07:00","id":950364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950231#post950231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, I'm very surprised that Prime appears to have absolutely nothing to do with &quot;perfecting&quot; substances given its redefined and emphasized purview (and I would love an answer to my earlier question concerning platonic forms and perfected materials)..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. How in the world is Prime completely unrelated to Thaumium or Sophis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T19:22:06-07:00","id":950381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950358#post950358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any Arcana can Perfect <i>examples of things under its purview</i>. That's what the Perfecting Practice does. The question is, is the process of turning (say) gold to orichalcum a matter of refining the molecular structure of the gold, or a matter of bringing the gold symbolically more in line with its supernal ideal? If it's the former, it should be Matter Perfecting. If it's the latter, it should be Prime Perfecting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The text for Honing the Form states that it is used to created Perfected Fire with the addition of Forces 3 and +2 Reach. I do not understand why a simple Forces 3 Perfecting spell, without any added Reach or other Arcana,cannot create Perfected Fire (or perfected light, sound, electricity, gravity, etc.)<br /> <br /> In fact, based on the purview of each Arcana as described in the core, I believe it should require Prime 3 (possibly plus Forces, Life or Matter, as may be applicable), to create a perfected <i>anything</i> (similar to the rules for transforming objects and beings),<br /> <br /> The only rationale for making Matter so necessary and central to the perfecting game is to emphasize Moros as &quot;alchemists&quot; and/or expand magical toy production beyond mostly Obrimos mages. If so, that reeks of &quot;game balance&quot; (and really confuses and weakens Prime as an Arcanum).<br /> <br /> For instance, why exactly does Twilight &quot;purify&quot; metals or anything else, and why can't Prime do so?<br /> <br /> I think perfected materials are a great addition to mage and definitely appreciate the direction taken in the spoiled text, but believe the 2e mechanics still need more work, clarity and consistency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 08-13-2016, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T19:34:20-07:00","id":950386,"title":"","content":"So if we're scrapping the idea of creating perfected metals by passing them through twilight, what alternative methods could we use?<br /> <br /> Perhaps a complex alchemical process of mixing the metal with certain forms of tass, and allowing it to cook in a hallow at 350 degrees until well done?<br /> <br /> If the kinds of tass required are obscure enough, it could give an explanation for why these metals aren't ubiquitous, and give extra value to hallows whose tass is compatible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-13-2016, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T19:51:07-07:00","id":950391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950386#post950386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if we're scrapping the idea of creating perfected metals by passing them through twilight, what alternative methods could we use?<br /> <br /> Perhaps a complex alchemical process of mixing the metal with certain forms of tass, and allowing it to cook in a hallow at 350 degrees until well done?<br /> <br /> If the kinds of tass required are obscure enough, it could give an explanation for why these metals aren't ubiquitous, and give extra value to hallows whose tass is compatible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's no need to scrap the twilight metal perfecting method, only explain the purification metaphysics other than that's how it was done in 1e.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a related note, if repeated jaunts to and from twilight (and/or consistent exposure to a strong hallow) cleanses and perfects objects, it begs the question of what it does to both mages and sleepers...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":".  typo 08-14-2016, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T20:15:19-07:00","id":950395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950391#post950391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no need to scrap the twilight metal perfecting method, only explain the purification metaphysics other that that's how it was done in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>As others have pointed out, this explanation has a lot of plot holes. It doesn't actually work with Death. It begs the question of why Werewolves don't have tons of perfected metal. It begs the question of why perfected metal is produced spontaneously in Hallows, rather than in Loci. It begs the question of why shifting a substance from ephemera to material and back would make it closer to a supernal ideal. It begs the question of why this method has nothing to do with Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-13-2016, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T20:19:03-07:00","id":950396,"title":"","content":"Let's say a character has a Dedicated Tool that is a mundane form of one of the Perfected Metals or Materials. I assume they could transmute it into the Perfected form and still use it as a Dedicated Tool?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T20:24:36-07:00","id":950403,"title":"","content":"Does Lunargent have antiseptic properties, like normal silver? Will water in a Lunargent vase never go bad?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-13-2016, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T20:35:20-07:00","id":950408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950395#post950395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It begs the question of why Werewolves don't have tons of perfected metal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to note that werewolves don't regularly enter twilight, they can perceive and sometimes affect spirits in twilight, and they travel to/from the Shadow. Twilight and the Shadow are not the same thing/place/state of being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950396#post950396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say a character has a Dedicated Tool that is a mundane form of one of the Perfected Metals or Materials. I assume they could transmute it into the Perfected form and still use it as a Dedicated Tool?</div> </div> </div> </div>A dedicated tool can be of any substance or nature. I believe you meant to inquire whether a Path tool can still be used as a Yantra if changed to its perfected substance. I would assume that it would not make any difference as the perfected versions still resonate with the appropriate supernal realm, e.g. an Acanthus can use a lunargent wand as a Yantra same as a silver wand.<br /> <br /> However, an Obrimos can make use of Path tool comprised of any perfected material, not just gold/orichalcum or even the classic metals. (Mage, p.121, Materials sidebar)<br /> <br /> In fact, I believe my Obrimos really needs a new adamant wand....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T20:44:47-07:00","id":950413,"title":"","content":"&quot;Perfected living material offer a +1 tool Yantra on spells to enhance or imbue themselves,&quot;<br /> <br /> Imbuing is an attainment, not a spell. Is this sentence implying that it's possible to imbue without the attainment?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950408#post950408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to note that werewolves don't regularly enter twilight, they can perceive and sometimes affect spirits in twilight, and they travel to/from the Shadow. Twilight and the Shadow are not the same thing/place/state of being.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but it doesn't have any practical relevance in this case. Taking an item into the shadow works just as well for creating perfected metal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A dedicated tool can be of any substance or nature. </div> </div> </div>I think his question was whether transforming the material of your dedicated tool would cause it to become un-dedicated.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T20:49:48-07:00","id":950418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950413#post950413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true, but it doesn't have any practical relevance in this case. Taking an item into the shadow works just as well for creating perfected metal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an assumption with no support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T20:55:15-07:00","id":950420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950418#post950418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an assumption with no support.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it's not. It says so right in the spoiler.<br /> <br /> &quot;She can cast the Matter 3 spell Hone the Perfected Form (below,) or she can repeatedly convert the base material to ephemera and back again, either by passing it into and out of Twilight or carrying it into and out of the Shadow or Underworld.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T21:01:24-07:00","id":950421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950420#post950420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No it's not. It says so right in the spoiler.<br /> <br /> &quot;She can cast the Matter 3 spell Hone the Perfected Form (below,) or she can repeatedly convert the base material to ephemera and back again, either by passing it into and out of Twilight or carrying it into and out of the Shadow or Underworld.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It also directly answers your werewolf question immediately after that sentence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T21:13:29-07:00","id":950428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950421#post950421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also directly answers your werewolf question immediately after that sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? It seems to me that a werewolf could easily produce perfected metal by accident, if they carried any small metal objects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T21:32:40-07:00","id":950431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950428#post950428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? It seems to me that a werewolf could easily produce perfected metal by accident, if they carried any small metal objects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Small metal objects made entirely out of one metal.<br /> <br /> When one of those metals is a liquid and another is the literal bane of your entire species and four of the remaining five are mostly found in alloys.<br /> <br /> And that's not even getting into the &quot;resting&quot; thing or the matter of how werewolf shapeshifting might affect the metaphysical processes that perfecting works through.<br /> <br /> &quot;A werewolf might easily inadvertently be carrying small objects made of pure iron, tin, copper, or lead on a significant majority of their trips into and out of the Shadow without changing their own form&quot; is kind of a goofy thing to assume would be anything like common.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-14-2016, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T22:01:29-07:00","id":950435,"title":"","content":"I don't see why a werewolf shapeshifting would in any way inhibit the creation of perfected metals. <br /> <br /> That said, that's certainly a rare enough instance that it'd be a plot point, not werewolves having tons of perfected metal or anything. As mentioned, the metals are rare enough in pure form that few werewolves have that metal to begin with, and likely don't always have it on them when they go into the Shadow and back. The ones most common are likely the rare Blood Talon actually willing to carry a silver weapon, or those few other trinkets that might be heirlooms or something.<br /> <br /> So, there certainly ARE werewolves with lunargent and other perfected materials, I'm sure, but it's definitely not 'tons of them', or a lot of it. Probably just enough to make a werewolf here or there that much more tempting of a Mystery...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T22:20:16-07:00","id":950441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950435#post950435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why a werewolf shapeshifting would in any way inhibit the creation of perfected metals.</div> </div> </div> </div>A process that is an exercise in strengthening sympathy and purity through the conversion of matter to ephemera and back probably isn't going to be unaffected by entanglement with a being that naturally exists in a weird half-straddled position between those two states when some reconfigurations of that being may cause the material to be subsumed into their flesh for a while, is the bulk of my point in that hypothesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T22:27:24-07:00","id":950442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950431#post950431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">another is the literal bane of your entire species</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is exactly why you'd want to have it ready to shiv the Pure when they come to bother you. After all, the Pure are more vulnerable to silver than the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;A werewolf might easily inadvertently be carrying small objects made of pure iron, tin, copper, or lead on a significant majority of their trips into and out of the Shadow without changing their own form&quot; is kind of a goofy thing to assume would be anything like common. </div> </div> </div>In the modern era, power cables use pure copper. Bullets use pure lead. Any werewolf who carries a cell phone charger and a spare magazine with him for a while should expect to end up with brontium and apeiron.<br /> <br /> In the past, coins would fit the bill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-14-2016, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T22:37:39-07:00","id":950450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950441#post950441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A process that is an exercise in strengthening sympathy and purity through the conversion of matter to ephemera and back probably isn't going to be unaffected by entanglement with a being that naturally exists in a weird half-straddled position between those two states when some reconfigurations of that being may cause the material to be subsumed into their flesh for a while, is the bulk of my point in that hypothesis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, if anything, I'd see it helping, having the material subsumed into something that shifts between the physical and ephemeral so innately. But really I'd just lean towards 'no or unnoticeable effect'; there's no mention of a mage using Matter magic with shapeshifting spells to subsume an object temporarily affecting it, so I don't think a werewolf's shapeshifting would either, and that's comparatively more 'natural'.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I still agree with the overall point that it's not enough to make the materials 'wide-spread' among werewolves. Present, but not wide-spread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T00:06:32-07:00","id":950462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950442#post950442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the modern era, power cables use pure copper. Bullets use pure lead.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Use&quot; is not &quot;are.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T01:30:26-07:00","id":950476,"title":"","content":"Obviously, the most likely material a Werewolf or Sin Eater might turn into its perfected form by accident is probably leather.<br /> Or is there any character of importance in the average campaign that doesn't wear a black leather trenchcoat?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T03:42:03-07:00","id":950494,"title":"","content":"If I recall this correctly the original reason why you had to pass material to and from Twilight was because that way you would burn off the base elements in it. After enough passes this would leave you with just the Perfected remains (and a lot less material). Twilight was supposed to be closer to the Supernal world than the Lie and that is why it would be a hostile environment to unpure material. At the moment I cannot quote a source, but it was in one of the few books from 1E that mentioned Perfected metals.<br /> Siderite deserves a special mention since if you used siderite from a meteorite (star metal) you would only need half the normal amount of passes into and out of Twilight, which meant you also required only half the initial amount of material. I mention this because the current document does not state any loss of material in the Perfecting process. I believe this has several potential consequences:<br /> - Twilight burning off base elements is no longer the process at work. This opens up possibilities.<br /> - Infusion with Supernal elements/energy is mentioned somewhere. This would lend credibility to the theory that Prime should be able to also Perfect materials.<br /> - Your cellphone charger will keep working when you frequently travel through Twilight with it and your gun will not suddenly misfire due to disintegrating bullets","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T07:44:23-07:00","id":950548,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about the Living Perfected materials and why you can't perfect the entire organism and there is one perfect explanation for that:<br /> <br /> Sympathy.<br /> <br /> Or, more specifically, <i>Connected</i> sympathy. An entire body (plus soul stones, familiars, etc...) has a <i>Connected</i> sympathy to the individual's soul and, on some level, *is* the soul. This poses a problem for when you want to perfect the body, because you would essentially be attempting to perfect a part of the soul as well. As parts of the soul are intensely interconnected (again, with <i>Connected</i> sympathy) and are essentially the same object, you can't just choose to perfect a part of it, to perfect a soul, you have to perfect the entire thing. Attempting to perfect the body means to try and perfect only a part of the soul and that change will simply not take.<br /> <br /> Parts of the body, on the other hand, possess only <i>Strong</i> sympathy to the soul and so can be perfected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 08-14-2016, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T08:12:59-07:00","id":950558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950548#post950548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about the Living Perfected materials and why you can't perfect the entire organism and there is one perfect explanation for that:<br /> <br /> Sympathy.<br /> <br /> Or, more specifically, <i>Connected</i> sympathy. An entire body (plus soul stones, familiars, etc...) has a <i>Connected</i> sympathy to the individual's soul and, on some level, *is* the soul. This poses a problem for when you want to perfect the body, because you would essentially be attempting to perfect a part of the soul as well. As parts of the soul are intensely interconnected (again, with <i>Connected</i> sympathy) and are essentially the same object, you can't just choose to perfect a part of it, to perfect a soul, you have to perfect the entire thing. Attempting to perfect the body means to try and perfect only a part of the soul and that change will simply not take.<br /> <br /> Parts of the body, on the other hand, possess only <i>Strong</i> sympathy to the soul and so can be perfected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it said you can't perfect any whole living entity, not just humans? Which also raises questions when considering plants, given that, for many of them, you can pull off a piece, stick it in the ground, and it turns into a new plant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T08:35:34-07:00","id":950568,"title":"","content":"The plants would be an interesting experiment. I would guess they count as separate entities as long as they contain in themselves the entire essence of what it means to be a &quot;plant&quot;, which would be the capability to grow into a new one. You have that capability, you are a whole entity.<br /> <br /> Maybe the reason for why things work this way is the capability of souls of living beings to cause self initiated change of themselves - that's practically the difference between Life and Matter as well and the reason why you can perfect a stone, when stones have representation in the dreamtime as well. The changes that living beings go through would erode the perfection they would possess. So yes, you can target living being with Life magic, even indefinitely. You can Perfect their body with a perfecting spell by imposing a bunch of symbols from the Supernal on the body, but you can never make the mundane substance more perfect without using magic as a Lasting effect, as you can with metals and other materials. Or, well, you could Ascend. And yes, other living animals can apparently too. Read the Wellspring chapter in <i>Astral Realms</i>. It also says nothing about Ascended stones.<br /> <br /> You can perfect a severed limb, because it no longer has a soul, or at least doesn't have a soul that can change itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T08:45:06-07:00","id":950573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950568#post950568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The plants would be an interesting experiment. I would guess they count as separate entities as long as they contain in themselves the entire essence of what it means to be a &quot;plant&quot;, which would be the capability to grow into a new one. You have that capability, you are a whole entity.<br /> <br /> Maybe the reason for why things work this way is the capability of souls of living beings to cause self initiated change of themselves - that's practically the difference between Life and Matter as well and the reason why you can perfect a stone, when stones have representation in the dreamtime as well. The changes that living beings go through would erode the perfection they would possess. So yes, you can target living being with Life magic, even indefinitely. You can Perfect their body with a perfecting spell by imposing a bunch of symbols from the Supernal on the body, but you can never make the mundane substance more perfect without using magic as a Lasting effect, as you can with metals and other materials. Or, well, you could Ascend. And yes, other living animals can apparently too. Read the Wellspring chapter in <i>Astral Realms</i>. It also says nothing about Ascended stones.<br /> <br /> You can perfect a severed limb, because it no longer has a soul, or at least doesn't have a soul that can change itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait... did I miss something new in second edition? I thought only humans and human based things had souls in mage (barring weird special cases due to powerful supernatural effects).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T09:07:36-07:00","id":950582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950573#post950573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait... did I miss something new in second edition? I thought only humans and human based things had souls in mage (barring weird special cases due to powerful supernatural effects).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing. The book for the realms is still a canon source in the 2E and everything written there can be considered as a part of the lore unless contested by information in 2E. The Astral Realms are the realms of the Soul. Although I think that, and that animals and even planets and stars have souls is a part of 2E corebook as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T09:34:50-07:00","id":950594,"title":"","content":"Wait, planets and stars and animals having souls? Could you cite things for this? This matters a lot, because, well, Death Sight literally can tell you if something has a soul or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T10:00:50-07:00","id":950607,"title":"","content":"That is... An iffy interpretation. Yes, everything, including animals, plants, rocks, etc. has a reflection in the Astral, which is in some interpretations the soul of the cosmos, with individual people's souls being parts of its greater whole. <i>However</i>, only humans (and supernatural templates that used to be human) have the things that can be seen with Death Mage Sight and interacted with using Death spells, that are composed of stuff related to the five subtle Arcana, that the game calls souls, and that cause the Soulless Condition when separated from the person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T10:25:53-07:00","id":950625,"title":"","content":"Only humans and certain posthuman beings (like mages!) have souls in the game-mechanical &quot;can see them and steal them with Death spells&quot; sense. Animals and rocks don't.<br /> <br /> Yes, the Anima Mundi is the collective soul of everything that doesn't have a soul. Yes, this makes sense.<br /> <br /> Well kinda. If you think about it.<br /> <br /> (Remember - the Temenos is in some ways an artificial construct of the Fall, like a lake formed by a dam, seperated from the Anima Mundi by the Omphalos. Did pre-Fall humans have souls as mages know them? Is the thing Death spells rip out someone's Temenos? Mysteries! I'm sure the Tremere would be happy to explain it to you...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T10:41:32-07:00","id":950633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950625#post950625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only humans and certain posthuman beings (like mages!) have souls in the game-mechanical &amp;quot;can see them and steal them with Death spells&amp;quot; sense. Animals and rocks don't.<br /> <br /> Yes, the Anima Mundi is the collective soul of everything that doesn't have a soul. Yes, this makes sense.<br /> <br /> Well kinda. If you think about it.<br /> <br /> (Remember - the Temenos is in some ways an artificial construct of the Fall, like a lake formed by a dam, seperated from the Anima Mundi by the Omphalos. Did pre-Fall humans have souls as mages know them? Is the thing Death spells rip out someone's Temenos? Mysteries! I'm sure the Tremere would be happy to explain it to you...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to reread the 1e Astral book, but damn this makes me want a 2e book on the Astral that covers Mages and Beasts!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T11:52:45-07:00","id":950674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950633#post950633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I need to reread the 1e Astral book, but damn this makes me want a 2e book on the Astral that covers Mages and Beasts!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Astral is a common element between enough gamelines that I will be <i>very</i> surprised if the Crossover Chronicle doesnt address it to some extent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T11:52:46-07:00","id":950675,"title":"","content":"Quick, everybody! Revive all the &quot;wtf is a soul?&quot; threads to discuss this!<br /> <br /> [joking...]<br /> [maybe]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T14:57:29-07:00","id":950761,"title":"","content":"As best I can understand, what your soul <i>is</i> is the thing that connects you to humanity as a whole. It's your twig that connects to the larger branch of the Temenos (and in turn to the trunk of the Anima Mundi). If you don't have a soul, you've effectively lost your Humanity Membership Card. Souls are interchangeable because as long as you've got <i>a</i> card, you're a human, and you get to participate in the club. Non-human beings don't have souls because they don't <i>need</i> souls. A dog can be a dog or a spirit can be a spirit without needing a soul that says they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T16:32:26-07:00","id":950787,"title":"","content":"Under Alloys, it says that perfected metals are chemically inert, but then in Apeiron it says that Apeiron is not chemically inert. Then in Orichalcum, it says that chemical inertness is Orichalcum's special ability, and gives a mechanical effect (immunity to non-magical durability loss). These contradictions need to be ironed out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T19:27:48-07:00","id":950861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=949986#post949986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think I'm going to remove the Lasting effect on Hone The Perfected Form; if you want a Perfected item that won't eventually revert, you have to make it the old-fashioned way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Get Matter 5 and will it into existence?<br /> <br /> But really, if that's done then how do you get the permanent items made of Perfected Flesh or Blood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","user":"shkspr1048","date":". 08-15-2016, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T19:29:08-07:00","id":950863,"title":"","content":"I find Brontium very interesting. The simple fact that Brontium is non-magical, and is a perfect conductor of electricity means that it can be used to create all kinds of energy-efficient magnet-based levitation devices, among other things. Start your own hoverboard company.<br /> <br /> Also, the fact that Brontium is a perfect conductor of heat means that holding it for too long could cause hypothermia as your body heat is quickly sucked away and delivered into the air. In fact, if it's a perfect conductor of heat, doesn't that mean that your body heat would be instantaneously sucked out? That offers interesting methods of assassination.<br /> <br /> The fact that Apeiron is a perfect insulator of heat means that its temperature can never be changed without magic, and that its temperature is insignificant because it can't warm or cool anything it touches anyway.<br /> <br /> Does siderite ignore armor as well as Durability? Can siderite cut through siderite?<br /> <br /> Does perfected leather itself have immunity to blunt trauma, or does it also confer this on its wearer? I'd expect the former, not the latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950462#post950462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Use&quot; is not &quot;are.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the difference? Does the fact that the pure copper is wrapped in rubber make it any less pure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T20:22:20-07:00","id":950881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950863#post950863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the difference? Does the fact that the pure copper is wrapped in rubber make it any less pure?</div> </div> </div> </div>I struggle to understand how you can read &quot;requires an object made entirely out of the intended Perfected metal's mundane counterpart&quot; and think a wrapping that's part of the cord doesn't matter to a supernatural process that runs in part on semiotics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T21:03:14-07:00","id":950896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950881#post950881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I struggle to understand how you can read &quot;requires an object made entirely out of the intended Perfected metal's mundane counterpart&quot; and think a wrapping that's part of the cord doesn't matter to a supernatural process that runs in part on semiotics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then how do you make Hermium at all? Without a container, it'll just run through your hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T21:11:38-07:00","id":950900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950896#post950896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then how do you make Hermium at all? Without a container, it'll just run through your hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are literally comparing &quot;I have a power cord, which is attached to its insulating cover for reasons of basic safety and efficiency and is considered a discrete object made of multiple substances&quot; with &quot;I put a liquid in a container for storing liquids.&quot;<br /> <br /> You are also now completely discarding the process of targeting a mass of mercury as a discrete object with a spell that turns it into ephemeral mercury and back as a method of Perfecting that metal.<br /> <br /> To what end are you doing these things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T21:39:12-07:00","id":950912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950900#post950900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are literally comparing &quot;I have a power cord, which is attached to its insulating cover for reasons of basic safety and efficiency and is considered a discrete object made of multiple substances&quot; with &quot;I put a liquid in a container for storing liquids.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see the difference. If I say &quot;I'm buying a soda&quot;, people know you're talking about buying the bottle/can as well. It's a discrete object made of multiple substances. But does the bottle make the soda impure? I don't think so. For the same reason, I don't think a cable's cover makes the copper inside it any less pure. If the cover does make the copper impure, then surely the bottle makes the mercury inside it impure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are also now completely discarding the process of targeting a mass of mercury as a discrete object with a spell that turns it into ephemeral mercury and back as a method of Perfecting that metal.<br /> <br /> To what end are you doing these things? </div> </div> </div>If you cast a spell on just the mercury, it'll fall out of the container and splatter on the ground in Twilight, which would certainly contaminate it. Besides, I was responding to the idea of bringing it back and forth through a portal to twilight/shadow, which would involve taking the bottle through as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-15-2016, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T21:39:42-07:00","id":950913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950863#post950863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the fact that Brontium is a perfect conductor of heat means that holding it for too long could cause hypothermia as your body heat is quickly sucked away and delivered into the air. In fact, if it's a perfect conductor of heat, doesn't that mean that your body heat would be instantaneously sucked out? That offers interesting methods of assassination.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what a perfect conductor of heat would do. It basically means that temperature equalizes across the material at the speed of sound in the material.<br /> <br /> For example: say you had a miles long wire of Brontium stretched out, if you heat one end, that heat spreads across the whole length at the speed of sound in Brontium (which is probably very high) meaning that the end you heated wont melt before the whole thing does, and you have that whole enormous surface area to disperse that heat.<br /> <br /> This allows for very efficient cooling and heat transfer systems. This property is arguably the more impressive one, because, as far as I know, there aren't any other materials that do this (if I'm wrong and there is a real material that does this, please tell me, as I would love to read about it). Meanwhile science keeps inventing electrical superconductors that work at higher and higher temperatures. Although it being an electrical superconductor is still amazing and is extremely in making some things science won't be able to make for a decade or more.<br /> <br /> Together Brontium and Apeiron allow construction of incredible heat channeling and blocking systems which would solve many engineering issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 08-15-2016, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T21:44:20-07:00","id":950917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950913#post950913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not what a perfect conductor of heat would do. It basically means that temperature equalizes across the material at the speed of sound in the material.<br /> <br /> For example: say you had a miles long wire of Brontium stretched out, if you heat one end, that heat spreads across the whole length at the speed of sound in Brontium (which is probably very high) meaning that the end you heated wont melt before the whole thing does, and you have that whole enormous surface area to disperse that heat.<br /> <br /> This allows for very efficient cooling and heat transfer systems. This property is arguably the more impressive one, because, as far as I know, there aren't any other materials that do this. Meanwhile science keeps inventing electrical superconductors that work at higher and higher temperatures. Although it being an electrical superconductor is still amazing and is extremely in making some things science won't be able to make for a decade or more.<br /> <br /> Together Brontium and Apeiron allow construction of incredible heat channeling and blocking systems which would solve many engineering issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if you were to grab hold of the brontium, the heat in your hand would be absorbed by the brontium, and transferred to the cooler air at a very fast rate. I would imagine that if you kept hold of it for too long, it would cause hypothermia as the heat in your body is continuously drained out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T21:47:36-07:00","id":950919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950912#post950912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the difference. If I say &quot;I'm buying a soda&quot;, people know you're talking about buying the bottle/can as well. It's a discrete object made of multiple substances. But does the bottle make the soda impure? I don't think so. For the same reason, I don't think a cable's cover makes the copper inside it any less pure.</div> </div> </div> </div>People know you're talking about the bottle or can as well, but they don't conceptualize the bottle or can as part of the soda. Conversely, the covering on an electrical cable is conceptually part of the cable. If it didn't have the covering, it wouldn't be an electrical cable, it would just be a copper wire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950912#post950912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you cast a spell on just the mercury, it'll fall out of the container and splatter on the ground in Twilight, which would certainly contaminate it. We were talking about bringing it back and forth through a portal to twilight/shadow, which would involve taking the bottle through as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter if the container goes with the mercury or not, it matters if the mercury is made of anything but mercury (it's not). Likewise, it doesn't matter if the rubber coating goes with the copper or not, it matters if the cable is made of anything but copper (it is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T21:50:21-07:00","id":950920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950919#post950919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People know you're talking about the bottle or can as well, but they don't conceptualize the bottle or can as part of the soda. Conversely, the covering on an electrical cable is conceptually part of the cable. If it didn't have the covering, it wouldn't be an electrical cable, it would just be a copper wire.<br /> <br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if the container goes with the mercury or not, it matters if the mercury is made of anything but mercury (it's not). Likewise, it doesn't matter if the rubber coating goes with the copper or not, it matters if the cable is made of anything but copper (it is).</div> </div> </div> </div>So are you saying that an electrical cable could be converted to Brontium by accident, or that it couldn't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T21:52:55-07:00","id":950921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950920#post950920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are you saying that an electrical cable could be converted to Brontium by accident, or that it couldn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>It couldn't, unless the coating was removed first (and then it wouldn't really be an electrical cable, or at any rate not a very safe one).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T22:31:14-07:00","id":950931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950917#post950917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you were to grab hold of the brontium, the heat in your hand would be absorbed by the brontium, and transferred to the cooler air at a very fast rate. I would imagine that if you kept hold of it for too long, it would cause hypothermia as the heat in your body is continuously drained out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans don't have perfect thermal conductivity though. So while the Brontium could cool the surface of the skin, it would then be up the the body's thermal conductivity to transfer more heat there to be conducted away. Additionally, the body has countermeasures against cold killing you this way. The body restricts blood flow (an important way heat moves around the body) to the area sacrificing the part to save the whole. This is why people usually get frostbite (small parts of the body freezing) long before they die of hypothermia.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> Also the air around the brontium is not a very good conductor of heat and would have the same problem removing that heat as a human body does (although it also has convection at its disposal) unless the Brontium has a massive surface area to dump all that heat into.<br /> <br /> Additionally, unless the air is below freezing, the person won't precisely get frostbite either.<br /> <br /> If you got them to wear a brontium shirt somehow maybe that could work, it would take some calculations to figure out what portion of the body you would need to cover given a specific set of surface area to mass ratio, and maximum bodyheat generation per unit mass for the target, and average external temperature and externally exposed surface area for the brontium (ignoring the thermal energy stored in the brontium itself). I really don't feel like figuring out the equation for that calculation is worth the answers it would give, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 08-15-2016, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T23:30:09-07:00","id":950949,"title":"","content":"How does one handle Mercury, it being liquid?<br /> <br /> <i>Magic</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T00:08:25-07:00","id":950958,"title":"","content":"I imagine that it would only take Matter 3 to make solid Hermium, and I similarly assume that using spells directly on perfected objects that alter their inherent nature and properties do not interfere with their perfected advantages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T00:30:40-07:00","id":950964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950861#post950861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Get Matter 5 and will it into existence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Matter 5 spell could be real solution. Masters are so low in numbers they will not trip in-setting economy. But we will still have maybe problem 'Why go to Temples of Time Before if I can just make you Adamantium Fortress from this skycrapper?'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950861#post950861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But really, if that's done then how do you get the permanent items made of Perfected Flesh or Blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>First tossing them to Twillight makes them semi-permament so they can be ended with process on next few takes of tossing in Twillight and getting them back?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T00:42:58-07:00","id":950968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950949#post950949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one handle Mercury, it being liquid?<br /> <br /> <i>Magic</i></div> </div> </div> </div><b>I think that risen problem <i>needs</i> addressing in rules</b> - <b>Is container around material stoping Perfecting of it?</b> If yes, Hermium cannot truly by made because you need to somewhere store Mercury before tossing it back and forth in Twilight. OR alchemist cast each time Matter 2 <i>Shaping</i> to make Mercury 'solid' in to cube of metal and use <i>Alchemist Touch</i> to not be poisoned by it. Hermium then becomes most hard metal to Perfecting.<br /> <br /> <b>If no, I can Perfect a can of soda or bottle of wine. I can also Perfect cable as whole</b> - and then <i>yes</i>, you will have modern werewolves with perfected cell phones with then or black leather trenchcoats.<br /> <br /> <b>We <i>really</i> need clear division where one thing is that thing to Supernal magic and where it is not.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-15-2016, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T01:04:24-07:00","id":950972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950949#post950949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one handle Mercury, it being liquid?<br /> <br /> <i>Magic</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Or by working on a cold winter's day in Canada. -40 C? Easy peasy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T02:42:53-07:00","id":951001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950968#post950968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>I think that risen problem <i>needs</i> addressing in rules</b> - <b>Is container around material stoping Perfecting of it?</b> If yes, Hermium cannot truly by made because you need to somewhere store Mercury before tossing it back and forth in Twilight. OR alchemist cast each time Matter 2 <i>Shaping</i> to make Mercury 'solid' in to cube of metal and use <i>Alchemist Touch</i> to not be poisoned by it. Hermium then becomes most hard metal to Perfecting.<br /> <br /> <b>If no, I can Perfect a can of soda or bottle of wine. I can also Perfect cable as whole</b> - and then <i>yes</i>, you will have modern werewolves with perfected cell phones with then or black leather trenchcoats.<br /> <br /> <b>We <i>really</i> need clear division where one thing is that thing to Supernal magic and where it is not.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Magic is clear enough. One simple solution is to have a container in the Fallen and a container in Twilight and put them in the same place, since they're in different frequencies of reality they can share the same space. You then shift the hermium from the jar in the Fallen into the jar in Twilight and back again as often as you need to.<br /> <br /> So no, a cable that's made with copper doesn't become brontium because it's not one discrete object made of copper it's a composite. Unless your ST decides otherwise, because ST discretion is a thing.<br /> <br /> You probably ought to stop demanding answers you don't actually need. It's rude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T02:49:14-07:00","id":951005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=951001#post951001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no, a cable that's made with copper doesn't become brontium because it's not one discrete object made of copper it's a composite. Unless your ST decides otherwise, because ST discretion is a thing.<br /> <br /> You probably ought to stop demanding answers you don't actually need. It's rude.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>literally</i> was risen in this very topic at least by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a> few posts above - so no, it's not 'don't need answer' thing, as text is unclear on this and can lead to at least two different game world's interpretations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T02:51:05-07:00","id":951007,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> Yes, it was, and the answer was also given in this thread without the need to demand official input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-15-2016, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T04:13:58-07:00","id":951035,"title":"","content":"Excuse me, I was thinking that we are talking on what should be in <i>final rules</i> in <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> coming from shared beta, not what is in the topic about it on forum. What I pointed is that this thing <u><i>should</i></u>be more clearly written in final book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-15-2016, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T08:06:33-07:00","id":951113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950968#post950968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hermium then becomes most hard metal to Perfecting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the concept of a pool or divot or channel that difficult to grasp?<br /> <br /> Like, there's absolutely nothing about being at ground level that conceivably stops the &quot;natural&quot; process of Perfection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T08:57:36-07:00","id":951137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=951035#post951035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excuse me, I was thinking that we are talking on what should be in <i>final rules</i> in <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> coming from shared beta, not what is in the topic about it on forum. What I pointed is that this thing <u><i>should</i></u>be more clearly written in final book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't necessary when the question has already been answered. Only objects wholely of the material to be Perfected May in fact be Perfected. Your actual question of, &quot;Then how do I Perfect Hermium?&quot; is easily answered without the need to have explicit rules written for it, especially when there are so many options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-15-2016, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T09:52:47-07:00","id":951171,"title":"","content":"If Hone no longer has lasting as an option, but Forge retains it, can an adept use Honing the Form to Forge Lasting alloys, or will it revert when the underlying spell runs out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T10:57:38-07:00","id":951205,"title":"","content":"The game is written from a perspective in which the players around a table are able to come to a general consensus about how things work without bogging down on minutiae; we can argue on the forums all we want about whether an electrical cable is its own object to the point that it can't be perfected or if it's copper inside a rubber container and so the copper can, and it has no bearing on the way the game would play at all. In actual play the ST and group comes down on one side or another of that question and the rules resolve just fine. The group can decide whether there's a metaphysically significant difference between metal in a box and a cable, and whether one or both are disqualifying and the rules are able to cope with it.<br /> <br /> Explicitly addressing that kind of edge case behavior adds word count for no reason. We do not need to agree about what counts and what doesn't for the rule to be both clear and workable in play. Allowing that level of discretion to the individual groups is better writing and better design, for this kind of game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","user":"Eolirin","date":". 08-15-2016, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T12:46:33-07:00","id":951255,"title":"","content":"Personally I'm curious what combining Kassiterum and Brontium would result in, as Tin + Copper was one of the big ways Bronze was made during the Bronze Age. It seems like the ancient Mages would probably have tried that combination at some point, especially after they found they couldn't make Perfected Bronze.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T14:59:05-07:00","id":951329,"title":"","content":"Brontium sucking the heat out of somebody was answered correctly by another.<br /> <br /> <br /> The issue of a cable versus a container of mercury is self-evident. A cable is an object composed of a wire, an insulator, and possibly, a covering. A container of mercury would be two objects, a container and a quantity of mercury. You could hold liquid mercury in your hand without any problems. Only the vapor and some compounds are toxic. All that is moot, however.<br /> <br /> It doesn't actually matter when you have to take the mercury out of the container or the strip the cable down to the wire. When you perfect the mercury, what are you going to do? Put it in a container until you have a use for it. As for the cable, you either want the additional conductivity within that cable or you plan on stripping the cable down to the wire to make use of the brontium in some other way.<br /> <br /> See the pattern yet? It doesn't matter. You have to do the exact same thing either way no matter the circumstances. Question circumstances that could matter. What about electroplated metal? I would treat it as an alloy. What about alloys? I assume you need pure metal unless you use magic. Pure being better than 99% by weight, I guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the accidental perfection, only gold, silver, and copper coins or jewelry actually fit the criteria given as objects composed entirely of a pure metal, along with any wrought iron object. The effects of the perfected metals would not be easily noticed by anyone not a mage and you would attract mages by creating this stuff so that explains why werewolves and sin-eaters never bothered. Iron is a bit more of an issue than the rest but as the objects would be larger and higher in durability it would take a long time. It is plausible it never happened.<br /> <br /> The process sounds a bit like tempering so perhaps it needs a more explicit connection. Perhaps the traveling back and forth has to be within a short period of time. After the rest period, if necessary, the back and forth must continue without a pause. Any deviation messes it all up and you have to start over. That would bring accidental perfections down to coins, jewelry, and other trinkets leading us back to rare and in small amounts because nobody wants to attract mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:19:33-07:00","id":952023,"title":"","content":"The container seems moot when you can hover materials with Matter Ruling to keep anything from touching it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:53:06-07:00","id":952102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=951329#post951329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The process sounds a bit like tempering so perhaps it needs a more explicit connection. Perhaps the traveling back and forth has to be within a short period of time. After the rest period, if necessary, the back and forth must continue without a pause. Any deviation messes it all up and you have to start over.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually how I assumed it worked when I first read the section, that it was essentially a tempering process, not just a cumulative number of times it had to be shifted from matter to twilight and back. That would indeed make accidental perfecting much more uncommon, and makes a lot of sense as a way to perfect something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T19:51:57-07:00","id":952227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=952023#post952023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The container seems moot when you can hover materials with Matter Ruling to keep anything from touching it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or use Forces to create a force field to hold it in place, or use Space to create a bubble of spacetime to hold it, or use Death to rob it of kinetic energy, etc. etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T21:33:15-07:00","id":952283,"title":"","content":"Aye, that was what I was wondering this whole conversation about Mercury; what's stopping you from just magicking up a ball of free-floating mercury, and passing that through? While certainly not as easy, what with more spells necessary, seems easier than passing it through channels. Freezing it by magic should work too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T06:50:19-07:00","id":952480,"title":"","content":"Don't even need magic really, mercury freezes at minus fourty degrees (Celsius), a bit warmer even. It's not that much of a stretch to use mundane tech.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T07:01:49-07:00","id":952483,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> <br /> Text mentions how using a Grimoire bound in blood and flesh changes casting from them (ritual time is not doubled). Will there be any clarification on how obtaining such a Grimoire using normal merit rules work? Basically, is Perfected Fleshbound Grimoire buyable with Grimoire merit, and if so, are the costs changed in any way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:15:12-07:00","id":952592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=952480#post952480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't even need magic really, mercury freezes at minus fourty degrees (Celsius), a bit warmer even. It's not that much of a stretch to use mundane tech.</div> </div> </div> </div>Liquid nitrogen works pretty well. Not too expensive and surprisingly easy to get a hold of. Heck, put a bowl of mercury in a cooler with some ice for a couple hours and it should be sold long enough to get in a dozen or so passes.<br /> <br /> Actually, would liquid Mercury even have Structure greater than 1 in the first place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:18:10-07:00","id":952594,"title":"","content":"Any details on Perfected Ice, or Dark Matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:34:49-07:00","id":952603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=952594#post952594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark Matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you even start to work out the properties?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:41:14-07:00","id":952607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=952603#post952603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would you even start to work out the properties?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, that's why it'd be interesting. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:51:23-07:00","id":952613,"title":"","content":"Maybe it just disappears. I mean, the only symbolism Dark Matter has is that we can't find it, so Perfected Dark Matter can't be found by anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:57:29-07:00","id":952617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=952613#post952613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it just disappears. I mean, the only symbolism Dark Matter has is that we can't find it, so Perfected Dark Matter can't be found by anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, we think it exists. Maybe the material version of Incognito Presence? And yes, I realize that makes it practically worthless as you'd forget where it was. Maybe car keys spontaneously Perfect into and out of it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:58:59-07:00","id":952618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=952483#post952483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a><br /> Text mentions how using a Grimoire bound in blood and flesh changes casting from them (ritual time is not doubled). Will there be any clarification on how obtaining such a Grimoire using normal merit rules work? Basically, is Perfected Fleshbound Grimoire buyable with Grimoire merit, and if so, are the costs changed in any way?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if pig flesh (to name any animal) is as useful in such an endeavor as human flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T16:58:04-07:00","id":952850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=952594#post952594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark Matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfected Shadows? I like the idea of Perfected Shadows being Dark Matter. I mean, it's be pretty hard to make it, but that's why it's cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T17:18:32-07:00","id":952864,"title":"","content":"I don't see anything difficult about sending shadows back and forth through Twilight...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T17:25:44-07:00","id":952870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=952617#post952617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet, we think it exists. Maybe the material version of Incognito Presence? And yes, I realize that makes it practically worthless as you'd forget where it was. Maybe car keys spontaneously Perfect into and out of it...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=952850#post952850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfected Shadows? I like the idea of Perfected Shadows being Dark Matter. I mean, it's be pretty hard to make it, but that's why it's cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>There seems to be some confusion here about the nature of dark matter. Some of the defining characteristics of dark matter are that it interacts with the gravitational force but not the electromagnetic force. (I don't think anyone knows if it interacts with the strong or weak forces.)<br /> <br /> Because it doesn't interact with the electromagnetic force, it doesn't interact with light, and thus is invisible. Additionally the electromagnetic force is what is responsible for matter being able to touch other matter, so this means dark matter is intangible, even to other dark matter.<br /> <br /> However we don't have any problem finding the stuff, there are giant galaxy sized blobs of the stuff (usually overlapping with actual galaxies but not always) that have their own gravity. Anything with that much gravity bends the trajectory of light in what is known gravitational lensing. This is just one way to find dark matter, search the sky for distortions without an object causing them. You can also see its effects in the structure of galaxies, and the universe as a whole.<br /> <br /> I doubt that the Matter Arcanum even registers dark matter as being Matter, as dark matter isn't really anything like baryonic matter (normal matter). Especially since there is probably dark matter all around us passing through us like we don't exist.<br /> <br /> Look up neutrinos for an even better understood form of matter which ignores the electromagnetic force.<br /> <br /> PS: Dark energy is something unrelated, and not just the energy form of dark matter or whatever some people might guess based on its name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 08-17-2016, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T20:58:35-07:00","id":952962,"title":"","content":"Personally, the idea that the material to be perfected is required to be <i>pure </i>is wacky on the face of it. Separating out the parts as part of the processing itself seems more alchemical to me.<br /> Also: Why would one physical process work on all materials to be perfected? (Making things work faster and better the more pure? Sure, that makes sense.)<br /> Why would multiple processes work on the same material the same way?<br /> <br /> That's hard to accept.<br /> <br /> <br /> I like Shadow/Material for Lunargent/Mithril but for Siderite less so and Orichalcum (Solargent?) less still. Perfecting Lead in Twilight makes sense while Shadow does not.<br /> <br /> The realms required for each should <i>vary</i>, which would give you some protection against over-proliferation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Toss in appropriate other specific perfection requirements. ('Lunargent requires no light for some number of passes and moonlight for the rest' if you want procedural types. 'Orichalcum must be purified in perfected Fire or it doesn't work.' might work for a material req..) The appropriate arcana should be good at ameliorating these.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, the werewolves running around with Lunargent weapons probably picked them up from a Lune... who may well grant useful rare gifts that help.<br /> <br /> My preference is for each material to have one or two thematic (and really annoying) requirements that one or both of the most appropriate arcana can overcome easily and one or two further requirements that require involved processing or difficult magic.<br /> <br /> In this case, Matter being able to straight up perfect almost any material with a spell <i>shouldn't </i>be Lasting. Prime should have some fun stuff along those lines, too. Life for the living, Forces for those, and so on.<br /> <br /> Somewhat like Summoning, the mages involved would be naturally inclined towards stuff from their path but anybody might make the stuff the hard way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T00:56:57-07:00","id":953028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=952962#post952962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orichalcum (Solargent?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Argent means silver, lunargent is literally moon silver.<br /> <br /> If you want to rename it to follow the pattern of lunargent, you might want to make a word that means sun gold. For example: 'solaurum' (which would be pronounced sole-or-um or perhaps so-lore-um (I think I like the sound of the second pronunciation better, it flows better)).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 08-18-2016, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:13:53-07:00","id":953226,"title":"","content":"How about Perfected Amber? Or foodstuffs. I could see an Iron Chef Adamant getting serious with awakened cuisine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T10:07:03-07:00","id":953260,"title":"","content":"I thought up a story to explain why the Free Council came up with the spell and the stuff is so rare. It is too long to fit in a book though when it amounts to ST fiat in an out of game context.<br /> <br /> I assume the metal requires a resonance with the Supernal to become Perfect which builds up in the form of a mystical vibration created by shifting states or realms. I think I remember reading somewhere it was the shifting that created the transformation. Anyway, the energy is a constant so normally requires constructive interference to build up the vibrations, 10 times followed by a day of resting to stabilize. The vibrations would be described in the form of a wave. If the build up of the waves follows a harmonic series then it would be difficult to discover the process without mage sight to tell what is going on, even more difficult if the waves dissipate over time. Perfect metals seem to have mystical and scientific qualities to separate them from the mundane so it makes sense for the process to have both mystical and scientific elements. Assuming the length of time spent shifted is a variable affecting the period of the wave and you have a simple process in practice but so complicated in theory that a general spell that works for all materials at any size (excluding nature of spell factors in that statement) instead of specific cases would not be easily crafted, hence the Free Council discovery and no accidental perfections.<br /> <br /> Ex: A gold ring is shifted into a Twilight state for a set period of time. The ring must be shifted 10 minutes later for the same amount of time then again 9 minutes after that and again 8 minutes after that, etc. all for the same amount of time each time. If you miss the first time window then you would wait an additional 10 minutes and would have some number of chances like this based on the time shifted.<br /> <br /> Deviation from the correct pattern creates destructive interference that destroys the wave and you would need to start over from the beginning. The precise numbers are irrelevant as it would be by ST fiat. This increases the variables to durability, size, and shifted time which could have its own variability based on realm/state of the shifting. Even if someone managed to accidentally achieve the result without any knowledge of what was going on during the process they would have a heck of a time recreating the occurrence and it would be of little help in figuring out how to do it with even a slightly different case, size/material. Historically, I think that puts it around 1800, but it would be 14th century for harmonics and maybe around 1700 for the underlying physics elements necessary for discovery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T10:29:50-07:00","id":953273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=953028#post953028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Argent means silver, lunargent is literally moon silver.<br /> <br /> If you want to rename it to follow the pattern of lunargent, you might want to make a word that means sun gold. For example: 'solaurum' (which would be pronounced sole-or-um or perhaps so-lore-um (I think I like the sound of the second pronunciation better, it flows better)).</div> </div> </div> </div>True, &quot;solarum&quot; would be a better fit. I plead severe headache. <br /> sO-lahr'-um or sO-lahr''-E'-um (solarium) would be my preferred pronunciations. <br /> <br /> I sympathize with not using orichalcum for gold, though. I don't know where that even came from, honestly. The first RPG I saw with the connection was Exalted.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T10:38:31-07:00","id":953278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=953273#post953273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sympathize with not using orichalcum for gold, though. I don't know where that even came from, honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Color and linguistic drift go a long way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T13:58:42-07:00","id":953414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=953273#post953273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, &amp;quot;solarum&amp;quot; would be a better fit. I plead severe headache. <br /> sO-lahr'-um or sO-lahr''-E'-um (solarium) would be my preferred pronunciations. <br /> <br /> I sympathize with not using orichalcum for gold, though. I don't know where that even came from, honestly. The first RPG I saw with the connection was Exalted.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, the exact same person that the myth of Atlantis came from. Seems appropriate to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T14:06:43-07:00","id":953418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=953273#post953273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, &quot;solarum&quot; would be a better fit. I plead severe headache.<br /> sO-lahr'-um or sO-lahr''-E'-um (solarium) would be my preferred pronunciations.<br /> <br /> I sympathize with not using orichalcum for gold, though. I don't know where that even came from, honestly. The first RPG I saw with the connection was Exalted.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Solarium is already a word, it is a room designed for maximum sunlight.<br /> I find it helpful to google any potential word I come up with to ensure it isn't already a word, which I don't know.<br /> <br /> I was basing the pronunciation on the Latin pronunciations; I said &quot;sol aurum&quot; really fast a bunch of times in a row until they mixed, to crudely simulate extended use and the accompanying pronunciation shift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T14:43:22-07:00","id":953431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=953414#post953414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funnily enough, the exact same person that the myth of Atlantis came from. Seems appropriate to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> Also, Aurichalcum is a valid spelling, if you want to tie Aurum into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T00:14:33-07:00","id":953701,"title":"","content":"Is anyone else confused about why the special physical property of kassiterum is basically just a lesser version of siderite's? Shouldn't it do something different, especially considering you can just amalgamate them to get both properties (which as it stands renders kassiterum's physical property useless)?<br /> <br /> Perhaps due to its use in solder, maybe kassiterum could bond to any mundane metal it touches, allowing it to act as a kind of metal glue?<br /> <br /> Also, as someone else already pointed out, there is a lot of inconsistency about whether all perfected metals are inert or just some. If they all are then perfected gold is missing a special property. Perhaps it could be tangible to things in twilight due to its connection to the Aether and the Aether's ability to cut through all layers of reality as stated in the description of the spell Ephemeral Enchantment. This would make perfected gold and perfected silver sort of complimentary.<br /> <br /> Also am I mistaken or is perfected water a better acid than perfected acid, because perfected water does the same thing as perfected acid except it doesn't randomly explode if you get it on the wrong thing? Also how fast do these work? Are they perfectly fast, such that if you were to spill some on your hand it wouldn't even have to slow down to dissolve a hole through your hand as it fell?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> Or a better idea for perfected gold would be that it reveals the the truth, a mirror would show things undisguised (the reflection a fast food ad would show the food as it really is before they cover it in paint and lacquer for example), if you listen through a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ear_trumpet\" target=\"_blank\">funnel</a> (or other sound affecting device) made from it you can't hear lies (or maybe even hear the actual truth) etc.<br /> <br /> It would be similar to Prime 1 Pierce Deception.<br /> <br /> It would only reveal the truth of things you would perceive in a normal version, if you want to see the truth of things in twilight you could amalgamate it with perfected silver.<br /> And perhaps a werewolf's reflection in a mirror made from this amalgam looks like all its forms superimposed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 08-19-2016, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T05:43:13-07:00","id":954318,"title":"","content":"You have slightly different uses for similar Perfect substances. Acid can come in a solid form at room temperature which helps when storing it and keeping it secret. Perfect HF would make an excellent poison. It would be readily absorbed by the skin and dissolve bones or stop the heart. At least you could walk away without anyone knowing something was up as opposed to melting a person with Perfect water. Normally strong acids and bases work immediately. The reasons they appear slow is they react with the water of the body (dilution) and form salts to impede penetration. I would assume them to work completely within minutes. Weak acids should take a little longer or more precisely have their secondary effects occur instead, like with HF.<br /> <br /> Kassiterum and Siderite have different ideal uses. Aside from the Yantra tool bonuses, one drains Essence from ephemerals while the other ignores durability. Kassiterum can be melted and molded so it makes for great weapons that lack an edge. Since you can't melt Siderite it needs to be the form you want or you will spend some serious time beating it into shape, best for blades and armor against corporeals.<br /> <br /> I guess a little more variation could be fine but I wouldn't want to lose anything in the process.<br /> <br /> As for inertness of metals, silver should be inert. I would suggest an equivalent of titanium for anything not meant to be reactive. It is corrosion resistant because it creates an inert oxide patina. That would prevent damage due to aging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 08-20-2016, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T06:27:13-07:00","id":954337,"title":"","content":"One thing about amalgams I am still not clear on is the properties of both metals. Does that mean you can add an additional perfect metal to the amalgam? Can you make Munchkin Metal by making an amalgam of all the Perfect metals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:03:52-07:00","id":954421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=954337#post954337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing about amalgams I am still not clear on is the properties of both metals. Does that mean you can add an additional perfect metal to the amalgam? Can you make Munchkin Metal by making an amalgam of all the Perfect metals?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One does not speak of producing Muchkitanium, lest all the other mages in the Consilium start to think of you as &quot;that guy...&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:27:56-07:00","id":954477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=954337#post954337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing about amalgams I am still not clear on is the properties of both metals. Does that mean you can add an additional perfect metal to the amalgam? Can you make Munchkin Metal by making an amalgam of all the Perfect metals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm not sure what would happen if perfected lead were combined with perfected copper (they're kind of opposites), but to my understanding, yes, its possible to combine them all.<br /> <br /> I there was a mention of something like that in the Forge Masters's write-up in Legacies the Ancient. They mention a metal call &quot;Electrum Magicum&quot; and say it is an alloy of all 7 Perfected Metals. In second edition, I don't know if it will be an alloy or an amalgam though, as they didn't, as far as I know, have Perfected Amalgams in first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:46:42-07:00","id":954490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=954421#post954421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> One does not speak of producing Muchkitanium, lest all the other mages in the Consilium start to think of you as &quot;that guy...&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm more the guy that knows &quot;that guy&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T22:07:00-07:00","id":954814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=953701#post953701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is anyone else confused about why the special physical property of kassiterum is basically just a lesser version of siderite's? Shouldn't it do something different, especially considering you can just amalgamate them to get both properties (which as it stands renders kassiterum's physical property useless)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at the end. Kassiterum also drains the essence from ephemeral entities.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:44:46-07:00","id":955102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=954814#post954814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at the end. Kassiterum also drains the essence from ephemeral entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I guess I wasn't clear enough in what I meant. Siderite, and Kassiterium both have two properties, Kassiterium's physical property is just a lesser version of one of Siderite's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T06:01:01-07:00","id":955541,"title":"","content":"Perfected oil would be fun. Sticking to any substance and burning perfectly leaving no residual substances after it's done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T13:59:47-07:00","id":957173,"title":"","content":"If I may, there's a rather simple explanation for why it would be difficult even for people regularly accessing the Twilight to accidentally make a lot of perfected material. You just have to consider that a &quot;treated&quot; material can't be perfected. There are very few materials in the modern world who do not come with their chemical treatment or some kind of coating. For instance, leather has chemicals used on them to help preserve them, iron has coating, ... (I have no scientific background so feel free to correct me here).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T14:46:59-07:00","id":957854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=957173#post957173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may, there's a rather simple explanation for why it would be difficult even for people regularly accessing the Twilight to accidentally make a lot of perfected material. You just have to consider that a &quot;treated&quot; material can't be perfected. There are very few materials in the modern world who do not come with their chemical treatment or some kind of coating. For instance, leather has chemicals used on them to help preserve them, iron has coating, ... (I have no scientific background so feel free to correct me here).</div> </div> </div> </div>By definition, leather is treated, so Perfected Leather should be impossible by that rule anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T04:15:09-07:00","id":958680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=955541#post955541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfected oil would be fun. Sticking to any substance and burning perfectly leaving no residual substances after it's done.</div> </div> </div> </div> Perfected oil/coal, zero carbon foot print because it burns completely, creating smokeless fire.<br /> <br /> Side effects include conjuring Jinn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T05:17:54-07:00","id":958695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=957854#post957854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By definition, leather is treated, so Perfected Leather should be impossible by that rule anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then :maybe ruling it needs to be untreated for the &quot;traditionnal&quot; method of goind back and forth throug Twilight but could be done through spells? That would also give a reason for the Free council developping a new spell (making perfected version of treated material) and at the same time would make being a Thyrsus slightly less efficient for making perfected materials: the perfected materials that Thyrsus can gather through their spells are slightly more difficult to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T09:53:03-07:00","id":958777,"title":"","content":"Would a suit of armor made from the right perfected materials and amalgams render someone invulnerable to almost all direct (non-spell) attacks?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> If so, and you combined this with some thaumium underneath and high Potency Wards and Signs (and maybe other anti-supernatural shielding effects), this would make the perfect unstoppable mage warrior.<br /> <br /> If this does work, why doesn't the adamantine arrow and seers have entire cabals decked out in this stuff as standard for their elite warriors?<br /> <br /> Or even the mysterium, no more getting eaten by nasty cryptids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 08-27-2016, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T10:12:08-07:00","id":958785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=958777#post958777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a suit of armor made from the right perfected materials and amalgams render someone invulnerable to almost all direct (non-spell) attacks?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> If so, and you combined this with some thaumium underneath and high Potency Wards and Signs (and maybe other anti-supernatural shielding effects), this would make the perfect unstoppable mage warrior.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it would.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=958777#post958777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this does work, why doesn't the adamantine arrow and seers have entire cabals decked out in this stuff as standard for their elite warriors?<br /> <br /> Or even the mysterium, no more getting eaten by nasty cryptids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Practicality. For one thing, people just don't walk around in suits of armor, particularly not in suits of metal armor. This is also going to require a significant quantity of a lot of precious metals to create, which is going to be extremely expensive, even to create a single suit. Then of course, it's going to be incredibly time-consuming and labor intensive to perfect, amalgamate, and alloy all these metals. Perfecting them will have to be done the old-fashioned way if you don't want the amalgams turning to piles of various metal and Mercury after a while, and perfected alloys just straight-up can't be made lasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T11:01:09-07:00","id":958807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=958785#post958785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Practicality. For one thing, people just don't walk around in suits of armor, particularly not in suits of metal armor. This is also going to require a significant quantity of a lot of precious metals to create, which is going to be extremely expensive, even to create a single suit. Then of course, it's going to be incredibly time-consuming and labor intensive to perfect, amalgamate, and alloy all these metals. Perfecting them will have to be done the old-fashioned way if you don't want the amalgams turning to piles of various metal and Mercury after a while, and perfected alloys just straight-up can't be made lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but as I described earlier in the thread, you can automate the perfecting process so perfected metals wouldn't be that rare.<br /> <br /> Plus this wouldn't be for average members, I meant people with like status 3 or more . A suit made from perfected amalgams would almost certainly be worth less than a mid range imbued item, and that alone would grant near immunity to physical attacks by cryptids and traps. Also it seems like the mysterium would be the most likely to be regularly going dangerous places where there aren't going to be many people to ask problematic questions.<br /> <br /> I can imagine a mid status mysterium cabal: &quot;Hey, we're going to investigate an ancient magical ruin, we need to borrow a few suits of armor, ok?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T15:11:38-07:00","id":958908,"title":"","content":"One idea that might be worth kicking around is an Abyssal equivalent to perfected materials - possibly made by corrupting perfected metals themselves. Not only does that give Scelesti their own dark toys to play with, but it provides an excellent in-game reason for why people don't walk around flaunting their Siderite armor or orichalcum jewelry. You're making a target of yourself, and your fellow mages won't <i>exactly</i> thank you for (inadvertently) helping the local Scelestic build a portal to the Abyss.<br /> <br /> (And yes, I used to watch the <i>Conan the Adventurer</i> animated series. How did you guess? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T14:55:08-07:00","id":959498,"title":"","content":"Wait alloys cant be made lasting? I think that's nerfing perfected materials a little to much. Sure make people have to make the base metals lasting through a long process witch i think should be some kinda laboratory ritual instead of passing back and forth through twilight but the alloys should at least be made lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T15:38:44-07:00","id":959524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hyperspacewizard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=959498#post959498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait alloys cant be made lasting? I think that's nerfing perfected materials a little to much. Sure make people have to make the base metals lasting through a long process witch i think should be some kinda laboratory ritual instead of passing back and forth through twilight but the alloys should at least be made lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have assumed that incorrectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T17:14:26-07:00","id":959577,"title":"","content":"I would think that perfected materials made the old fashion way would be lasting, while those made with the Free Council spell would not.<br /> \u200bShouldn't perfected Abyssal materials be materials that never existed?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T23:08:03-07:00","id":959681,"title":"","content":"I was thinking it was that Perfected Materials cannot be made Lasting on to itself with spell only, but <u>Alloys</u> of Perfected Materials are Lasting if components materials are Lasting. <br /> <br /> If you have Sodium and Chloride, you can get Salt. Problem with Perfected version of recipe is to get Perfected Sodium and Perfected Chloride, <i>not</i> Perfected Salt, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T02:47:09-07:00","id":964864,"title":"","content":"I'm firmly in the &quot;tempering&quot; camp - that it takes an active/deliberate effort to perfect a material. It just fits the metaphysics of the setting better.<br /> <br /> When <b>Mage</b> talks about &quot;Supernal truths&quot;, its putting a magical twist on a philosophical concept known either as &quot;universals&quot; or &quot;Platonic forms&quot;. Its a cool concept - if you're into philosophy - but the basic idea is that all mundane (Fallen) objects are just bad imitations of &quot;perfect&quot; versions that exist on some higher plane of existence.<br /> <br /> Take a look at gold, for example. According to <i>Mage'</i>s metaphysics, the stuff you buy at the jewelry store isn't actually &quot;gold&quot;. Instead, its a crude imitation of the Platonic form of &quot;gold&quot;, clumsily built out of totally unrelated bits of matter like &quot;protons&quot; and &quot;neutrons&quot;. As a result, all sorts of extraneous (or &quot;junk&quot;) properties are present, interfering with the true/magical properties of &quot;gold&quot;.<br /> <br /> So orichalcum isn't merely some enchanted form of everyone's favorite yellow metal. Its a radical new state of matter, created by systematically stripping the mundane metal of every principle and component that isn't found in <i>both</i> the physical and spirit realm versions of the stuff. The mage is actively pushing it into something as close to the idealized universal/Platonic form/Supernal manifestation as possible - if a mundane scientist could examine orichcalcum (or any other perfected material), they'd be talking Nobel prizes and revolutionary breakthroughs in materials science.<br /> <br /> Exactly what that means will depend on your campaign, but you can get some possible ideas by looking at neutrons. Neutrons are subatomic particles that serve primarily to stick the protons in an atom together - under the current model, they contribute <i>nothing</i> to the nature of the material itself. So, from a Platonic form/Supernal perspective, they're just garbage getting in the way - something the mage will have to rip out to get orichalcum.<br /> <br /> Now - assuming your game ever gets that detailed - this could mean that orichalcum has a radical new form of nucleus, laid out so that its stable with only a fraction of the neutrons that mundane gold has. Or maybe it has no neutrons whatsoever. Heck, maybe it doesn't even have a composite nucleus at all - perhaps the perfecting process has replaced the traditional nucleus with an exotic new form of subatomic particle.<br /> <br /> Which is probably why it takes magic to create alloys of the perfected metals. In perfecting the metals, the mage has removed the chemical properties that normally allow them to be alloyed, or to otherwise (chemically) react with other substances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":".  slight tweak for clarity 09-10-2016, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T12:39:36-07:00","id":965804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=958777#post958777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a suit of armor made from the right perfected materials and amalgams render someone invulnerable to almost all direct (non-spell) attacks?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> If so, and you combined this with some thaumium underneath and high Potency Wards and Signs (and maybe other anti-supernatural shielding effects), this would make the perfect unstoppable mage warrior.<br /> <br /> If this does work, why doesn't the adamantine arrow and seers have entire cabals decked out in this stuff as standard for their elite warriors?<br /> <br /> Or even the mysterium, no more getting eaten by nasty cryptids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, they do!<br /> <br /> It's only a 3-dot merit. Of course, it's vulnerable to dispelling then (I think), but you can't have everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:39:14-07:00","id":967124,"title":"","content":"As for why mages can't perfect machines?<br /> <br /> Well, metaphysically/philosophically, there's no inherent reason why they shouldn't be able to. Computers, cars, cellphone chargers - there should be a Platonic form for all of them. So, in principle, perfecting one <i>should</i> be possible.<br /> <br /> And in-game, there's certainly support for the idea. The second attainment of the Forge Masters, &quot;Primal Tempering&quot;, allows them to create a sort of poor-man's perfected machine. Detailed in <b>Legacies: the Ancient</b>, it uses the example of a typewriter to explain how it works. The attainment strengthens the core (Platonic form) properties of the typewriter, allowing . . . oh, say, a ghost to type a story on it. But it does nothing to help if you decide to bash someone upside the head with said typewriter - the fact that it can be used as an impromptu club is an incidental (&quot;junk&quot;) property, and thus not affected by Primal Tempering.<br /> <br /> However, the fact that Primal Tempering requires the mage to reshape his soul hints at the problem. Outright perfecting a machine may simply be too complicated for a normal mage. After all, if you just perfect the components, you'd probably wreck the machine, since perfecting metals alters their conductivity (etc.). A mage with enough Science/Engineering skill could probably come up with a design the can benefit from the altered physical properties of the perfected metals. But trying to do it without those skills would probably fry your cellphone, start a fire, or worse.<br /> <br /> And that's not the same thing as perfecting the actual machine. Now, its not hard to imagine the properties of a perfected cellphone charger. It would (almost) instantly charge any cell phone (regardless of manufacturer), using only a fraction of the power of a normal one, the cords would never tangle or break . . . But getting the cell phone charger into such a perfected state would be a nightmare. You'd have to preserve the charger's ability to convert AC into DC, simultaneously ramp the resistance both up <i>and</i> down, lock in perfect shape memory . . . Looking through the lists (both old and new) of perfected materials, <i>none</i> of them have those properties, and some of them seem to be mutually exclusive. If a perfected metal would get mundane scientists talking about a Nobel prize, a perfected machine would get mages talking about the same.<br /> <br /> Now, some techgnostic cabal or other will probably figure out a way to perfect a machine . . . eventually. It'll probably result in a new Legacy, and possibly require multiple mages working in concert . . . But that will take time - and complex machines are relatively new. Remember, electric machines (for example) are only about a hundred years old. By comparison, humans have been working with the (known) perfectable materials since prehistory. Thousands of years, after all, is a <i>lot</i> of time to get good with a particular skill","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:42:01-07:00","id":967434,"title":"","content":"So umm...I hate to bring this back up, and maybe open a few wounds but I do have a few questions.<br /> 1. How does Dumanium alloy scavenge Mana?<br /> 2. I thought I heard that Alloys can't be made permanent anymore that the spell has to end at some point, is that true?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:45:57-07:00","id":967436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div cl